@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmt:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/traditions/> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix pmw:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/works/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV:
# Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005)
#
# The harvest of the fourth Stupen', kept apart from traditions/transerfing.ttl,
# which declares the tradition and its works. The whole Stupen' was read,
# chapters XVI and XVII of the combined edition (Ves, 2012), in its English
# translation; the nodes follow the chapters. The text layer has no page
# numbers; every source names chapter and section heading.
#
# Two independent passes over two parts with reconciliation, then one
# integrator per part reading the whole part (prima-materia#924). Parts:
# chapter XVI; chapter XVII. Shared system terms are typed once, by the part
# that introduces them. The harvests of Stupen' I to III
# (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl to -3.ttl) are linked, not repeated.
#

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV:
# Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), part 1: chapter XVI Dances with Shadows.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 148 records, B 225;
# 52 records of B without counterpart in A: 4 added, 43 covered, 5 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 3 records both passes missed (the two laws
# of the pendulum as a systematization, the fading of works whose pendulums
# went out, and the order of cutting the tie before a new round of play) and
# corrected 3 (two attestations from third-party ascription to the author's
# own text, one prior step re-linked). One framing record is merged into
# pmc:TranserfingSteeringRealityWithoutDirectForceCh16. Stupen' I to III
# (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, -2.ttl, -3.ttl) are not restated: 11
# records whose claim a node there already carries are left out and linked;
# 21 nodes that restate an earlier node with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingPendulumRuleCh16,
# pmc:TranserfingStabilisingTheStructureCh16, pmc:TranserfingIndigoArrivalsCh16,
# pmc:TranserfingEnergyLordsCh16, pmc:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionCh16.
# The terms of part 2 (chapter XVII: the waking dream, the dream theatre, the
# Toltec cocoon and assemblage point, the two sides of reality) are not
# referenced; where this chapter borrows Castaneda's shifting of the
# assemblage point, it is described inside pmc:TranserfingTheLineAsIllusionCh16.
# The polemics against occult fears about sex and against church mediation are
# concepts, since only the author's side is read.
#

#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Origin of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingControlOfOnesOwnRealityAsPrimaryNeedCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control of one's own reality as the primary need"@en, "Lenkung der eigenen Wirklichkeit als Grundbedürfnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that the root drive of every living being is to steer its own life and bring its reality under its will; survival and reproduction are said to be derived from this drive, and it is named the origin of all intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Boredom is declared non-existent; what exists is a never-satisfied wish to master one's surroundings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Origin of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGameAsModelOfControllableRealityCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Game as a model of controllable reality"@en, "Spiel als Modell beherrschbarer Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Toys, games, spectacles, dreams and fantasies are explained as ways of rehearsing mastery: each turns a piece of independent reality into something that obeys the player's wish, which is why people retreat into them."@en ;
    skos:note "Everyday reality is said to feel mundane not because it is dull but because it resists control."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Origin of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSteeringRealityWithoutDirectForceCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Steering reality without direct force"@en, "Wirklichkeitslenkung ohne direkte Einwirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability, announced as the subject of everything that follows, to make the world come halfway to meet one's desires instead of pushing on it linearly; Transurfing is presented as the author's technique for steering reality without direct impact, in earnest rather than as play."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Contrasted with direct influence by immediate contact ('give it to me'). The English sentence calling direct influence 'by far the most effective' looks like a translation slip for 'not the most effective'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Origin of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'
#

pmc:TranserfingUnderstandHowRealityIsMadeBeforeControllingItCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Understand how reality is made before controlling it"@en, "Erst verstehen, wie Wirklichkeit entsteht, dann lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learning to control reality is said to require at minimum an understanding of how reality is formed, since each person creates their own world-layer without knowing the mechanism."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSteeringRealityWithoutDirectForceCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingLayerOfOnesWorld ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfContainedVersusComparativeEvaluationsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-contained versus comparative evaluations"@en, "In sich ruhende versus vergleichende Bewertungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Judgements like loving or disliking someone stand alone and are said not to polarise; judgements built on a condition or a comparison (I love you if you love me; I am good because you are bad) polarise and draw their opposite like magnet poles."@en ;
    skos:note "Used to explain incompatible spouses, the one difficult person in every group, and Sod's law."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingConditionalRelationships: an inflated evaluation that stands alone is held harmless; only once it is set against another does polarisation arise, and the balanced forces it raises act mainly against its maker. The excess potential (pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial) and the balancing forces (pmc:TranserfingUravnoveshivayushchieSily) are linked, not retyped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLawOfBadLuckAversionDrawsItsObjectCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of bad luck: aversion draws its object"@en, "Gesetz des Pechs: Abneigung zieht ihren Gegenstand an"@de ;
    skos:definition "A thing given special meaning through comparison is said to attract objects with opposite qualities; aversion makes a person a magnet for whatever irritates them. Illustrated by neighbours: they do not suffer from you because they attach no importance to you, while your irritation supplies the energy that brings ever new nuisances. Polarisation is said to bend the energy field so that reality's reflection warps as in a curved mirror."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to be natural, not mystical; the neighbours' neighbours can amplify the effect when their feelings coincide."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWhatYouHateFollowsYou: the pull of what one dislikes is traced here to polarisation born of comparison, and named the law of bad luck."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGeneralisedAversionCanBringDisasterCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Generalised aversion can bring disaster"@en, "Verallgemeinerte Abneigung kann Unglück anziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disliking neighbours as a whole category is said possibly to attract graver harm, e.g. flooding or fire."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLawOfBadLuckAversionDrawsItsObjectCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing's chief rule: self-acceptance and letting others be"@en, "Hauptregel des Transerfing: sei du selbst und lass andere sie selbst sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The main rule of Transurfing. Steps: allow yourself to be as you are, which means accepting yourself with every imperfection; allow others to be as they are, which means withdrawing what you expect of them and have hung on them; relax the grip on the world and give it freedom; stop insisting on desires and rights; deliberately change your attitude to the situation according to this rule rather than pushing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRefrainingFromComparisonOthersCh15: the formula is named here the main rule of Transurfing, set against the pendulum rule (pmc:TranserfingPendulumRuleCh16), and said to remove polarisation at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPressingAndInsistingWorsensMattersCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pressing and insisting worsens matters"@en, "Drängen und Beharren verschlimmert die Lage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fighting the outside world instead of removing polarisation is warned against; the harder one insists on one's wishes and rights, the stronger the opposite is drawn in, so forcing a situation only makes it worse."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDroppingTroublesomeNeighboursFromOnesLayerCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping troublesome neighbours from one's layer"@en, "Lästige Nachbarn aus der eigenen Weltschicht entfernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: for a while forget the neighbours; stop judging them; act as if they did not exist; tell yourself to dismiss them ('to hell with them'); remove them from the layer of your world and so detach the suction of the dependent relationship."@en ;
    skos:note "Applies the main rule (A1-12) to the neighbour case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReleaseFromPolarisationDrivenTroubleCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from polarisation-driven trouble"@en, "Befreiung von polarisationsbedingten Problemen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which a dependent relationship is broken, the polarisation is gone and the related nuisances fade; the rule is said to free anyone who keeps it from many otherwise inexplicable problems and to make life welcoming and pliable."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated in this section and repeated at the start of 'Everything Happens to Spite You'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMainRuleYieldsReleaseFromPolarisationCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Main rule yields release from polarisation"@en, "Hauptregel bewirkt Befreiung von Polarisation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping the main rule of Transurfing is said to remove polarisation and the problems it attracts."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseFromPolarisationDrivenTroubleCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingNeighboursYieldsReleaseFromNeighbourTroubleCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping neighbours yields release from neighbour trouble"@en, "Nachbarn loslassen bewirkt Ende des Nachbarschaftsärgers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Removing the neighbours from one's layer is said to end their polarisation so they gradually stop bothering one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDroppingTroublesomeNeighboursFromOnesLayerCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseFromPolarisationDrivenTroubleCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeighboursStopBotheringMayEvenBecomeFriendsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neighbours stop bothering, may even become friends"@en, "Nachbarn stören nicht mehr, werden womöglich Freunde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: once the relationship is detached the neighbours gradually cease to trouble you; if the dependency is broken completely, something unexpected may happen and the former nuisances may turn into close friends."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDroppingTroublesomeNeighboursFromOnesLayerCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Law of Bad Luck'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'
#

pmc:TranserfingClaimThatRuleNeverFailsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Claim that the rule never fails"@en, "Behauptung, die Regel wirke ausnahmslos"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author asserts that the Transurfing rule works unfailingly: releasing control at once makes life welcoming and pliable."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is held to be; no test procedure given here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotLettingGoKeepsOneMagnetForOppositesCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not letting go keeps one a magnet for opposites"@en, "Wer nicht loslässt, bleibt Magnet für das Gegenteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "without releasing one's grip one goes on attracting the opposite of what one wants, and the clash of opposites escalates beyond Sod's law."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: without releasing one's grip one goes on attracting the opposite of what one wants, and the clash of opposites escalates beyond Sod's law; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhyOppositesKeepFightingCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why opposites keep fighting"@en, "Warum Gegensätze im Streit bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The textbook law of unity and struggle of opposites is reinterpreted: balanced forces bring opposites together to restore balance, but the continuing fight between them is left unexplained by that alone and is attributed to pendulums."@en ;
    skos:note "Reinterpretation of the dialectical law, not an explicit dispute with a named author."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOppositesUnited: beyond bringing opposites together, the forces are said to keep them fighting, which pendulums sustain."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJumpingJesterIrritationFeedsDisturbanceCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The jumping jester: irritation feeds disturbance"@en, "Der hüpfende Narr: Gereiztheit nährt Störung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Image for the escalation in which, once nerves are strained, outer disturbances multiply in proportion to the irritation: obstacles when in a hurry, noisy people when one wants peace, visitors when one wants solitude."@en ;
    skos:note "People who cause the disturbance are said not to act on purpose but from subconscious motives steered from outside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsCh16 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums"@en, "Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invisible informational-energetic entities that arise from what living creatures think; like leeches they sense polarisation, feed on conflict energy and, through the subconscious, push people to emit more of it. They are held to lack conscious intention and cannot reach clear awareness."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to be a universal source of evil; most are destructive to some degree, some relatively harmless. The Transurfing pendulum is named as one needed so that many people start to reflect."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMayatnik: pendulums are said to sense polarisation as leeches sense blood, to steer subconscious motives so that people give off still more conflict energy, and to be the universal source of evil."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "informational-energetic entity feeding on conflict energy" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSleepingWhileAwakeCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sleeping while awake"@en, "Schlaf im Wachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people act automatically with little sober awareness; awareness is said to be lowest at home and in crowds and somewhat higher among a small circle outside the home. Uncontrolled subconscious choices, such as the small swerves of a walker, are where pendulums act."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrated by the pedestrian who steps into your path each time you try to overtake."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWakingLifeAsDozingCh7: awareness is graded by setting, lowest at home and in a crowd, higher in a small circle away from home."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAdmittedLimitsOfPendulumExplanationCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Admitted limits of the pendulum explanation"@en, "Eingestandene Grenzen der Pendelerklärung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author stresses that the mechanism is not fully understood, that pendulums and balanced forces act without premeditation, and that how a specific pendulum appears and acts can never be fully answered; only regularities are being noted."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how firm the model is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLawOfThePendulumCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of the pendulum"@en, "Gesetz des Pendels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once equilibrium forces make opposites clash, pendulums are said to do everything to inflame the conflict; under resistance events move toward escalation despite temporary truces, and reason has no power. Explains senseless quarrels, sudden coldness between partners, inexplicably cruel crimes and wars over belief."@en ;
    skos:note "Communities such as an army, gang or sect with fixed patterns of behaviour are said to numb the mind and open it to the zombifying effect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up from sleep in waking"@en, "Erwachen aus dem Schlaf im Wachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: notice how pendulums are trying to steer you right now; stay out of their destructive battles unless they matter to you personally; in a crowd step off the stage into the audience, survey the scene and wake; question why you are present, what you are doing, whether you see what is going on; state the waking formula precisely: right now I am awake, fully aware of what I do and why I do it this particular way."@en ;
    skos:note "The wording of the waking statement is said to need to be exact."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7: the waking statement is given a fixed wording, and the step serves to stay out of pendulum battles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulumManipulationCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from pendulum manipulation"@en, "Freiheit von Pendelmanipulation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting with awareness so that pendulums lose their hold; their power is said to vary inversely with awareness and to last only while one sleeps in waking. With awake consciousness things no longer happen to spite you."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpYieldsFreedomFromPendulumsCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up yields freedom from pendulums"@en, "Erwachen bewirkt Freiheit von Pendeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The waking procedure is said to remove the pendulums' power over one's actions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulumManipulationCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWithoutAwarenessOneStaysPuppetCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Without awareness one stays a puppet"@en, "Ohne Gewahrsein bleibt man Marionette"@de ;
    skos:definition "lacking this awareness, one is a puppet even in the most trivial conflict; it is hardest to keep when something annoys you."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: lacking this awareness, one is a puppet even in the most trivial conflict; it is hardest to keep when something annoys you; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignOfCaptureJesterKeepsJumpingCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of capture: the jester keeps jumping"@en, "Zeichen der Verstrickung: der Narr hüpft weiter"@de ;
    skos:definition "as long as nerves stay on edge and disturbances keep multiplying, the pendulum's loop holds your attention and one has been drawn into its game of raising conflict energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: as long as nerves stay on edge and disturbances keep multiplying, the pendulum's loop holds your attention and one has been drawn into its game of raising conflict energy; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16, pmp:TranserfingFreeingAttentionFromPendulumsNooseCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuppressingEmotionDoesNotWorkCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Suppressing emotion does not work"@en, "Gefühle unterdrücken nützt nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not reacting at all is said to be nearly impossible, and suppressing emotions is useless; switching attention is recommended instead."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChangeAttitudeNotEmotion: the remedy offered here is moving attention elsewhere, not a changed attitude."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFreeingAttentionFromPendulumsNooseCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSwitchingAttentionYieldsFreedomFromPendulumCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Switching attention yields freedom from the pendulum"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitswechsel bewirkt Lösung vom Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redirecting attention is said to free one from the pendulum's loop."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFreeingAttentionFromPendulumsNooseCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulumManipulationCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoisyNeighboursGraduallyQuietenCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Noisy neighbours gradually quieten"@en, "Laute Nachbarn werden allmählich leiser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: once attention is occupied elsewhere the neighbours will gradually become quieter."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingFreeingAttentionFromPendulumsNooseCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFreeingAttentionFromPendulumsNooseCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Freeing attention from the pendulum's noose"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit aus der Pendelschlinge lösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: do not try to stop reacting or suppress emotion; shift attention to something else; e.g. against disliked neighbour music put on your own music just loud enough to mask it, not louder; find other things to occupy your mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Indifference would also free one but is said to be hard to reach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNothingHappensToSpiteYouWhenAwakeCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nothing happens to spite you when awake"@en, "Nichts geschieht mehr zum Trotz, wenn man wach ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: with this awareness all will be well, and events stop turning against you once consciousness is awake."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Everything Happens to Spite You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'
#

pmc:TranserfingSexualComplexesAsPendulumMadeIllusionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sexual complexes as pendulum-made illusion"@en, "Sexuelle Komplexe als von Pendeln erzeugte Täuschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nobody is said to be neutral toward sex; unrealised or failed intention there produces negative slides. Pendulums, aided by the media, are said to persuade people that only they have problems, while in fact nearly everyone has some."@en ;
    skos:note "Freud mentioned only to set him aside, no dispute."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFlashPendulumCh16 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Flash-pendulum"@en, "Blitzpendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The briefest kind of pendulum, arising from momentary synchronous action (flash mob, stadium wave, concert audience, two people in the sexual act); it feeds on resonance energy that would be spent anyway and is held to be harmless."@en ;
    skos:note "The entity other cultures place over the sexual act and label with charged symbols is identified with it. On stage, a performer's call to join in feeds such a pendulum, which is said to take most of the energy."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "flash-pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "short-lived resonance-feeding pendulum" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumRuleCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How pendulums form: 'copy me' as rule"@en, "Wie Pendel entstehen: die Regel ›Mach es wie ich‹"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using the flash mob as the briefest and harmless case, the author explains that when a group thinks alike its uniform thought energy forms a resonance that a pendulum absorbs; durable pendulums need an agreed code of conduct and thought. Rules are made by people; pendulums arise from them spontaneously. The 'copy me' rule ('do as I do') is called humanity's most harmful creation."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed by this part (Russian pravilo mayatnika). Differs from pmc:TranserfingRuleFollowingFeedsPendulum: the rule comes first and gives birth to the pendulum, and 'do as I do' is called humanity's most harmful creation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstOccultFearsOfEntitiesFeedingOnSexCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against occult fears of entities feeding on sex"@en, "Gegen okkulte Furcht vor Wesen, die sich vom Sexualakt nähren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some occultists are reported to hold that the sexual act draws subtle-plane beings into an orgy of their own; the author answers that there is nothing to fear, since only a harmless flash-pendulum is involved."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the author's side is given; the occult view is paraphrased by him, no named author, so it is entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMediaAsCarrierOfPendulumRuleCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Media as carrier of the pendulum rule"@en, "Medien als Träger der Pendelregel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Digital media are said to condition behaviour and thinking with standards of success, especially in intimacy; no one plans it, it happens automatically, because people doubt themselves and compare, so they adopt others' success as their benchmark."@en ;
    skos:note "The author hesitates over the word 'zombify' but says this is the direction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhySexGoesWrongRolePlayComparisonForcedCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why sex goes wrong: role-play, comparison, forced mixing"@en, "Warum Sexualität misslingt: Rollenspiel, Vergleich, erzwungene Vermischung"@de ;
    skos:definition "following the standard model means altering and betraying oneself; partners pick roles and project expectations, watch themselves like spectators and compare with the norm, whereas sex needs relaxation, freedom and total immersion; trying to fuse love and sex artificially gives an awkward hybrid; fear of one's 'animal' side waters it down with ritual and inhibition."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: following the standard model means altering and betraying oneself; partners pick roles and project expectations, watch themselves like spectators and compare with the norm, whereas sex needs relaxation, freedom and total immersion; trying to fuse love and sex artificially gives an awkward hybrid; fear of one's 'animal' side waters it down with ritual and inhibition."@en ;
    skos:note "Lack of sexual fulfilment is named as the main underlying cause of separations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffectionAggressionScaleOfLoveAndSexCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Affection-aggression scale of love and sex"@en, "Skala Zuneigung–Aggression für Liebe und Sex"@de ;
    skos:definition "A scale with zero in the middle: deflection toward affection is love, toward aggression is sex; the two are distinct, may combine or stand apart, and sex is said to lean more toward aggression than affection."@en ;
    skos:note "Strong aggression is said to trigger a need for reassurance ('do you love me?')."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfArrowCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go of the arrow"@en, "Den Zeiger loslassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: drop the standard models; stop pulling the affection-aggression pointer to either side; let it swing freely according to the heart's feelings rather than the mind's ideas; set your own criteria of humanity and decency instead of others'; release the pointer as deliberately as you used to hold to the rule."@en ;
    skos:note "Addressed especially to couples who love each other and have sexual difficulties."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLettingGoOfArrowYieldsReliefOfSexualCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go of the arrow yields relief of sexual problems"@en, "Zeiger loslassen behebt sexuelle Schwierigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Releasing the affection-aggression pointer is said to be all that is needed to remove the problem."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfArrowCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingConflictFreeIntimateRelationshipCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOpenSpeechInRelationshipCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Open speech in a relationship"@en, "Offenes Sprechen in der Beziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: name things plainly without mixing up notions; be clear about what you want from the relationship; tell your partner; behave openly, assuming your partner has hidden wishes too."@en ;
    skos:note "Life is said to get easier at once when one acts openly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRejectingPendulumRuleCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rejecting the pendulum rule"@en, "Die Pendelregel verwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: stop following 'do as I do' standards entirely and put the Transurfing rule in their place."@en ;
    skos:note "In couples: accept yourself as you are with all imperfections; withdraw the projection of your expectations from the other."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromComplexesBeforeSexualFulfilmentCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from complexes before sexual fulfilment"@en, "Freiheit von Komplexen vor sexueller Erfüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fulfilment in sex is said to require feeling free and uninhibited, which is impossible while carrying excess potential such as an inferiority complex."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingConflictFreeIntimateRelationshipCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingComplexesVanish ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Balanced forces prevent relaxing, however hard one tries." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConflictFreeIntimateRelationshipCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conflict-free intimate relationship"@en, "Konfliktfreie intime Beziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sexual relationship in which tension from dependency and projection is gone and situations where one partner wants what the other rejects resolve by themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Even with complexes still present the Transurfing rule is said to lower tension noticeably, as it neutralises the polarisation of the dependent relationship at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingResolvingIncompatibleWishesInACoupleCh16 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Resolving incompatible wishes in a couple"@en, "Unvereinbare Wünsche im Paar auflösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordered procedure for a couple where one wants what the other finds unacceptable."@en ;
    skos:note "Earlier in the passage the first principle of Frailing (pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12, already carried in Stupen' III) is numbered first and the rule second; the closing restatement gives the order used here."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:TranserfingRejectingPendulumRuleCh16 ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "First drop the pendulum rule, then adopt the Transurfing rule in its place, then aim intention according to the first principle of Frailing." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeStepCoupleProcedureYieldsConflictFreeRelationshipCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The three-step couple procedure yields a conflict-free relationship"@en, "Paarverfahren bewirkt konfliktfreie Beziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rejecting the pendulum rule, applying the Transurfing rule and directing intention by Frailing are said to free the couple from further problems."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRejectingPendulumRuleCh16, pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16, pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingConflictFreeIntimateRelationshipCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoFurtherProblemsInCoupleCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No further problems in the couple"@en, "Keine weiteren Probleme im Paar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: tension drops noticeably, the clash of wishes resolves on its own, and if both partners do it they should have no more problems."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingRejectingPendulumRuleCh16, pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16, pmp:TranserfingReplacingTheIntentionToReceiveWithTheIntentionCh12."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorksWithoutExplainedMechanismCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Works without explained mechanism"@en, "Wirkt ohne erklärten Mechanismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author declines to explain why the couple procedure works, leaving that to psychologists, and simply asserts that it does; the first principle of Frailing is likewise said to work every time even without being understood."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is held to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSurrogateSuccessAndOwnPathCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surrogate success and the own path"@en, "Ersatzerfolg und der eigene Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Standards of success offered by the pendulum rule are called a substitute and a mirage; another's success cannot be copied, and true success is said to come only to those who dare to break the rules and follow their own way."@en ;
    skos:note "Pendulums are said to exist because of the rule, not to make it; their destructive core is diverting people from the path to their happiness. Illustrated by figures in black forcing passers-by into a marching line and by the film The Matrix."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDoNotFollowOthersPathsX10: the standards of success are called a surrogate that the pendulum rule hands out, and the illusion is said to be kept because it is sweeter and easier than the unknown."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChasingModelsOrWallingThemOffBothFailCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing models or walling them off both fail"@en, "Vorbildern nachjagen oder sich abschotten scheitert beides"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two failing responses to not matching the standard: chasing the model and remaking oneself brings only dissatisfaction, like a donkey after a carrot, and radiates energy destructive pendulums feed on; building a wall of rejection costs as much energy and is hard to keep up under constant bombardment by rules."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Two failing responses to not matching the standard: chasing the model and remaking oneself brings only dissatisfaction, like a donkey after a carrot, and radiates energy destructive pendulums feed on; building a wall of rejection costs as much energy and is hard to keep up under constant bombardment by rules; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWalkingOnesOwnPathCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWalkingOnesOwnPathCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking one's own path"@en, "Den eigenen Weg gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: decline to follow the pendulum rule; stop measuring yourself by standard models; go your own way, living by your own rules and for your own pleasure."@en ;
    skos:note "People with disabilities, having nothing to lose, are said often to manage this and to be happier than teenagers copying a sports star."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerFreedomCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner freedom"@en, "Innere Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A rare and striking quality gained by those who refuse the pendulum rule and go their own way."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnPathYieldsInnerFreedomCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own path yields inner freedom"@en, "Eigener Weg bewirkt innere Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Refusing the rule and walking one's own path is said to give inner freedom."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWalkingOnesOwnPathCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerFreedomCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFearOfBeingDifferentBlocksInnerFreedomCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of being different blocks inner freedom"@en, "Angst vor dem Anderssein verhindert innere Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "From a reader's letter (a woman near thirty, by choice without sexual experience, starting to feel abnormal under social pressure): the author says she stands short of inner freedom only because she still fears being unlike others; advice is not to fear it, to be glad of it without excess, and perhaps to lower her expectations."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: From a reader's letter (a woman near thirty, by choice without sexual experience, starting to feel abnormal under social pressure): the author says she stands short of inner freedom only because she still fears being unlike others; advice is not to fear it, to be glad of it without excess, and perhaps to lower her expectations; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWalkingOnesOwnPathCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheLineAsIllusionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The line as illusion"@en, "Die Reihe als Täuschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "What makes the pendulum harmful above all is said to be that it draws people off the road to their own happiness: as when figures in black force passers-by into a marching rank, standing in the line comes to seem reality. The text inverts this: the demand to stand in line is the illusion, and the real fact is that one may leave it. Telling the two apart is said to need a strong jolt."@en ;
    skos:note "The film The Matrix is offered as science fiction converging on fact. For the jolt the author borrows Carlos Castaneda's image of shifting the assemblage point, a third-party figure used here without further account."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoubtTurnsRuleBreakersIntoOutcastsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt turns rule-breakers into outcasts"@en, "Zweifel macht Regelbrecher zu Ausgestoßenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breakers of the pendulum rule end up either leaders or renegades; the outcasts fail because they still doubt their right to break it, while the leaders know they have it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Breakers of the pendulum rule end up either leaders or renegades; the outcasts fail because they still doubt their right to break it, while the leaders know they have it; it bears on pmp:TranserfingWalkingOnesOwnPathCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Pendulums are said to adopt a rising star as favourite and build a new rule around it, so the line turns to follow the new model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSteppingOutOfLineWithoutStruggleCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stepping out of line without struggle"@en, "Ohne Kampf aus der Reihe treten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: do not resist the enforcers; step out of line calmly, smiling and waving them farewell; go your own way; whatever pressure follows, avoid any conflict with them."@en ;
    skos:note "They are said to be powerless if one does not engage in conflict."@en ;
    skos:note "Fighting the enforcers is futile: pmc:TranserfingOpenRevolt (Stupen' I), linked, not repeated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLeavingWithoutFightYieldsInnerFreedomCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving without a fight yields inner freedom"@en, "Kampfloses Austreten bewirkt innere Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stepping out of line without conflict is said to leave the pendulums unable to pull one back."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSteppingOutOfLineWithoutStruggleCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerFreedomCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReviseOnesWorldviewFirstCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Revise one's worldview first"@en, "Erst das Weltbild überdenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "To grasp how to leave the line one must first rethink one's present view of the world; Transurfing is said to set things right and help resist the rule."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingSteppingOutOfLineWithoutStruggleCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingSurrogateSuccessAndOwnPathCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Pendulum Rule'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'
#

pmc:TranserfingStabilisingTheStructureCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Second law of the pendulum: stabilise the structure"@en, "Zweites Pendelgesetz: die Struktur stabilisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides inflaming conflict, every pendulum is said to strive to keep and strengthen the structure on which its existence depends; it forms together with an ordered structure of living beings, synchronises its adherents through direct and feedback links and acts like an algorithm, not a reasoning mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Evidence offered: instant synchrony of fish schools and bird flocks (telepathy ruled out because separate fish do not react), coordination in ant colonies unexplained by pheromones. Self-organisation is held to apply only to inanimate matter such as crystals; how the pendulum organises is said to be unknown."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed by this part (Russian vtoroi zakon mayatnika). Its first law: pmc:TranserfingLawOfThePendulumCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGroupBehaviourAsPendulumsOuterProgrammeCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group behaviour as the pendulum's outer programme"@en, "Gruppenverhalten als äußeres Programm des Pendels"@de ;
    skos:definition "An isolated creature follows its own instincts; in a group the pendulum's external programme steers the whole, the more so the lower the awareness. The predatory world is traced to the first law; aggression is therefore not held necessary to nature (New Zealand cited)."@en ;
    skos:note "People bond when 'swinging on the same pendulum'; cities such as Caral in Peru, without weapons or walls, are offered as stabilising pendulum structures that may grow into civilisations until a flaw brings them down."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCitiesAsPendulumHierarchiesCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cities as pendulum hierarchies"@en, "Städte als Pendelhierarchien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Offered as the most striking case of the second law: the oldest cities, such as Caral in Peru, which shows no weapons, pottery or defences, are said to have arisen because a pendulum structure formed spontaneously and stabilised the settlement. A city is called a layered pendulum hierarchy of making, consuming and exchanging; if stable at the outset it grows, possibly into a civilisation, until a flaw in its architecture brings it down."@en ;
    skos:note "Second law: pmc:TranserfingStabilisingTheStructureCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIsolationKeepsAwarenessStructureInducesSleepCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Isolation keeps awareness, structure induces sleep"@en, "Abgeschiedenheit erhält Gewahrsein, Struktur schläfert ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living apart, a person stays responsible for their own acts; as an element of a structure they largely sleep and must obey the pendulum rule, producing a conflict between personal interest and the structure's demands. Enlightenment is said to have been reached by those who withdrew from society."@en ;
    skos:note "Worst case: toiling for the system without ever lifting one's head to become aware."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBorrowedStrengthInExchangeForObedienceCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Borrowed strength in exchange for obedience"@en, "Geliehene Kraft gegen Gehorsam"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where an individual lacks inner support, the pendulum offers strength but only in return for submission to the structure's rules; the seemingly confident leaders of a group hang on its hook, others copy them and so the structure forms; adherents comply unconsciously."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrated by teenagers in summer camps living in a waking sleep like a non-lucid dream, by everyday swearing, and by a court that stopped washing after its king. The rule is said able to legitimise any absurdity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheRuleLegitimisesAnyAbsurdityCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The rule legitimises any absurdity"@en, "Die Regel rechtfertigt jeden Unsinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adherents keep the rule without awareness and take it to be right; as long as all do the same, any absurdity passes: swearing turns into ordinary speech, and a French court that stopped washing after its king covered the stench with perfume and took up little sticks for scratching. Whoever first coins a catchword is a shepherd; those who repeat it in chorus are sheep."@en ;
    skos:note "Pendulum rule: pmc:TranserfingPendulumRuleCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSecurityInStructureCostsIndividualityCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Security in a structure costs individuality"@en, "Sicherheit in einer Struktur kostet die Individualität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shelter in a structure gives peace, but the price is one's individuality and the soul's uniqueness on which one's genius rests; heart and mind can no longer unite and, fully in the structure's power, one cannot hear the heart's voice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWithdrawalChangesNothingIfOneStillSleepsCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Withdrawal changes nothing if one still sleeps"@en, "Rückzug ändert nichts, wenn man weiterschläft"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's own path need not lie outside every structure; retreating to the mountains is useless if life there remains an unaware waking dream. The task is to stay master of one's fate inside the structure."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIsolationKeepsAwarenessStructureInducesSleepCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGainingConfidenceInsideGroupWithoutSubmittingCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gaining confidence inside a group without submitting"@en, "Selbstvertrauen in der Gruppe ohne Unterwerfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: wake up; while still on the stage watch the scene as an onlooker, noting who are the pendulum's favourites and who are mere followers; do not judge or look down on those who follow the rule; do not merely reject the rule but put the Transurfing rule in its place; find the source of strength and security inside yourself."@en ;
    skos:note "Example given: a child in a group who needs self-confidence without becoming either a follower or an outcast."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7: the onlooker's stance is used to see who in a group are the pendulum's favourites and who its followers, so as to gain confidence without submitting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwakenedWhoLookDownBecomeOutcastsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The awakened who look down become outcasts"@en, "Erwachte, die herabblicken, werden ausgestoßen"@de ;
    skos:definition "if awareness leads you to compare yourself with the 'sleepers', a dependent relationship and polarisation arise and the one who woke up inevitably becomes an outcast."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: if awareness leads you to compare yourself with the 'sleepers', a dependent relationship and polarisation arise and the one who woke up inevitably becomes an outcast; it bears on pmp:TranserfingGainingConfidenceInsideGroupWithoutSubmittingCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRejectionOfRuleNeedsTransurfingRuleInItsCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Rejection of the rule needs the Transurfing rule in its place"@en, "Verwerfen der Pendelregel braucht die Transerfing-Regel als Ersatz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rejecting the pendulum rule alone is said to be insufficient; only when replaced by the Transurfing rule can inner strength and security be found."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingInnerStrengthAndCalmSelfConfidenceCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObserverStanceYieldsInnerStrengthCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Observer stance yields inner strength"@en, "Beobachterhaltung bewirkt innere Stärke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking up as an onlooker inside the group and applying the Transurfing rule is said to give strength and security from within."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGainingConfidenceInsideGroupWithoutSubmittingCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerStrengthAndCalmSelfConfidenceCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerStrengthAndCalmSelfConfidenceCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner strength and calm self-confidence"@en, "Innere Stärke und ruhiges Selbstvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A steady, calm trust in oneself and strength and security drawn from within rather than borrowed from a pendulum; lack of confidence is traced to fear of the unknown, so understanding the game already brings it halfway."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Also described as living by one's own convictions."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti: calm confidence is traced here to knowing how the game works, since its lack is fear of the unknown."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidWakingDreamMasteryOfSituationCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid waking dream: mastery of the situation"@en, "Bewusster Wachtraum: Herr der Lage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living life as a conscious waking dream, which is equated with having control of the situation; one becomes a shepherd or at least stops being a sheep, and decides consciously whether to keep or refuse a structure's rules while others sleep."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChoosingTheScriptAwakeCh7: the waking dream is reached here through knowing how pendulums act, and its mark is deciding while others sleep."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpYieldsLucidWakingDreamCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up yields the lucid waking dream"@en, "Erwachen bewirkt den bewussten Wachtraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Awareness of how pendulums work is said to enable living as in a lucid waking dream with control of the situation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLucidWakingDreamMasteryOfSituationCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingGuiltAndSelfProofYieldsInnerStrengthCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping guilt and self-proof yields inner strength"@en, "Schuld und Selbstbeweis ablegen bewirkt innere Stärke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ceasing to justify oneself and to defend or prove one's worth, together with the Transurfing rule, are said to suffice for a sense of inner strength and security."@en ;
    skos:note "The two steps are those of pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13 (Stupen' III), to which the author refers back; they are linked, not repeated."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingStopJustifyingCh13, pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerStrengthAndCalmSelfConfidenceCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotBlindlyFightStructureCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not blindly fight the structure"@en, "Die Struktur nicht blind bekämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rashly opposing a structure in a desperate attempt to shake off its influence is warned against; the aim is not total freedom from pendulums but not being their puppet, deciding consciously which rules to keep."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOpenRevolt: the warning concerns structures, and the awake person is to decide consciously whether to keep or refuse their rules."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLucidWakingDreamMasteryOfSituationCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPromotionByFitNotMeritCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Promotion by fit, not merit"@en, "Aufstieg nach Passung, nicht nach Leistung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A system is a pendulum that begins as ideas and principles and then takes material form; it places people by how well they fit and serve its stability, not by quality of work. What counts is doing things 'correctly' from the system's view, not 'well'."@en ;
    skos:note "In most teams creativity and initiative are welcome; in management apparatus and large firms corporate ethics value discipline and diligence, and initiative may be punished."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAdvancingInSystemBySupportingItsStabilityCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Advancing in a system by supporting its stability"@en, "Im System aufsteigen durch Stützen seiner Stabilität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: wake up early; recognise what kind of pendulum your team is; learn the difference between doing well and doing correctly; aim your actions first at supporting the system's stability; act consciously and flexibly according to its rules, being 'more correct' rather than 'better' in corporate settings."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to be less hard than it looks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCareerAdvancementWithinStructureCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Career advancement within a structure"@en, "Karriereaufstieg innerhalb einer Struktur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rising in one's career or a power hierarchy by fitting the system's criteria of correctness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSupportingStabilityYieldsAdvancementCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Supporting stability yields advancement"@en, "Stabilität stützen bewirkt Aufstieg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Aligning with the system's stability and its notion of correctness is presented as the way up."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAdvancingInSystemBySupportingItsStabilityCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCareerAdvancementWithinStructureCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Stabilising the Structure'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'
#

pmc:TranserfingIndigoArrivalsCh16 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Indigo children"@en, "Indigo-Kinder"@de ;
    skos:definition "A new type of child, said to bear an indigo aura and to have appeared since the early 1970s; held to be independent, dignified, sure of their worth, wise and aware beyond their age, intolerant of authority, sensitive to excess potential and falsity, led by the heart more than the mind. Generational renewal is said to be speeding up, the Indigos' own children already going beyond them. The author takes them as a response of balanced forces to the global pendulum network, as if fulfilling a predetermined mission."@en ;
    skos:note "Term from the clairvoyant Nancy Ann Tappe; described in Carroll and Tober's book the book 'The Indigo Children', used here as authority, not as a received text. Their disobedience is called unintended action of balanced forces against imposed discipline."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed by this part (Russian deti indigo); it names the section 'The Indigo Arrivals'."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Indigo children" ;
    pm:nameRole "new generation counterbalancing pendulum domination" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumNetworkAsMatrixCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The pendulum network as matrix"@en, "Das Pendelnetz als Matrix"@de ;
    skos:definition "Information and telecommunication systems are said to have grown a planet-wide network of pendulums; people slot into its cells, are wrapped in conditioned patterns and believe they act freely while able to want only what serves the structure. The process of enslaving will is called synergetic, i.e. self-organising, since pendulums lack conscious intention."@en ;
    skos:note "This calls the process self-organising, whereas 'Stabilising the Structure' restricts self-organisation to inanimate nature; the tension is left unresolved in the text."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingInformationMatrixCh13: the network is said to enslave the will itself, teaching people to want what the structure needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstChurchMediationCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against church mediation"@en, "Gegen kirchliche Vermittlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing Carroll and Tober that Indigo children find the present church hard to accept and feel themselves children of God, the author asks whether they need intermediaries to God and answers that they hardly do."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the author's side is given; the church is not quoted, so it is entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInwardAttentionRaisesAwarenessCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inward attention raises awareness"@en, "Nach innen gerichtete Aufmerksamkeit steigert Gewahrsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Awareness is said to rise when attention points inward and to sink into unconscious play when the mind is absorbed in worries imposed from outside."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as the source of the Indigo children's wisdom; a reincarnation-based role reversal between parents and children is floated as a question."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDivinePowerOfUnitedHeartAndMindCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divine power of united heart and mind"@en, "Göttliche Kraft: Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Children are said to be born with the Creator's power to create a new reality, rooted in unity of heart and mind, together with independence, awareness, intuition and individuality; pendulums, ruling by 'divide and rule', sever heart from mind and the gifts are lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Transurfing is offered as help to regain at least part of this God-given strength in this life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHowChildrenLoseTheirGiftsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How children lose their gifts"@en, "Wie Kinder ihre Gaben verlieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pendulum world keeps showing children their imperfection; suspicion then fear become habitual, standing out risks exclusion, so they merge into the structure and gradually lose independence, awareness, intuition and individuality."@en ;
    skos:note "The outcome of the struggle between structure and independence is said to be undecided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'The Indigo Arrivals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'
#

pmc:TranserfingTrueGoalsOnlyInNaturalHabitatCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "True goals only in the natural habitat"@en, "Wahre Ziele nur im natürlichen Lebensraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every creature is said to have its own goal whose pursuit drives evolution; it can be reached only in its natural setting. Domestication subordinates goals to the structure; man, building structures, enslaves himself too and forgets what he wants."@en ;
    skos:note "Wild deer contrasted with farm cows; likened to selling one's soul to the devil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyLordsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy market and energy credit"@en, "Energiemarkt und Energiekredit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The super-structure pendulum cares only about energy, the prime product; any fulfilled need radiates energy. Alcohol is called energy on credit: euphoria is the advance, the hangover the repayment with interest, during which the pendulum drains free energy; since will depends on free energy, the debtor loses will, which is named the main cause of alcoholism. The first credit is the most generous."@en ;
    skos:note "Felt as ticks in the heart-chakra area of the energy body. Drugs give the greatest yield; tobacco, coffee, tea, soft drinks and chewing gum are lower-interest credits."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed by this part: the pendulums as lords of the energy market, naming the section 'Energy Lords'. Free energy: pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyCreditFromSubstancesCanKillCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Energy credit from substances can kill"@en, "Energiekredit aus Rauschmitteln kann töten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repayment is never waived; growing debt brings harsher payback, the heart may stop, and survival is luck; the slide is unnoticed at first and then snowballs irreversibly. Anyone taking such a loan must stay highly aware and realistic about their 'creditworthiness'. Tempting but harmful things end badly."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingEnergyLordsCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStreetDrunksAsUnpaidDebtorsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Street drunks as unpaid debtors"@en, "Straßentrinker als säumige Schuldner"@de ;
    skos:definition "People drinking on the street are said to be not morally fallen but debtors who misjudged their resources, failed to repay the energy credit in time and keep taking new loans that are ever harder to repay; the fall goes unnoticed at first, then gathers into an irreversible snowball, the vortex of an induced shift that can pull in anyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Induced transition: pmc:TranserfingIndutsirovannyPerekhod (Stupen' I); energy credit: pmc:TranserfingEnergyLordsCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDependencyAsCapturedAttentionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dependency as captured attention"@en, "Abhängigkeit als gefangene Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Addiction is said to arise not mainly from physiology but because the arrow of intention or attention gets snared in the pendulum's loop, like a song stuck in one's head; the debtor's thoughts keep circling around the next portion."@en ;
    skos:note "Evidence offered: heavy smokers on a submarine mission do not crave while smoking is impossible; internet or game addicts lose withdrawal symptoms on return to the screen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillPowerSeldomFreesFromDependencyCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Will power seldom frees from dependency"@en, "Willenskraft befreit selten aus Abhängigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Effort of will alone is said rarely to release attention from the loop, just as a tune leaves one's head only when replaced by another."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingHabitByChangingScriptAndSceneryCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBreakingHabitByChangingScriptAndSceneryCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking a habit by changing script and scenery"@en, "Gewohnheit brechen durch Wechsel von Drehbuch und Kulisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: switch attention to something else rather than relying on will power; identify the script and setting that go with the habit (e.g. the smoke break at work); change that script and scenery, using a little imagination, having first truly wanted to."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to be the only way and not hard."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingIndifferentPartingFromHabitCh13: release comes from changing the script and scenery tied to the habit, not from parting with it indifferently."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromHarmfulHabitsCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from harmful habits"@en, "Freiheit von schädlichen Gewohnheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Release from dependency, figured as paying off all debts and leaving the pendulum's bank."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChangingScriptAndSceneryYieldsFreedomFromHabitsCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Changing script and scenery yields freedom from habits"@en, "Wechsel von Drehbuch und Kulisse bewirkt Freiheit von Gewohnheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changing the habit's script and setting is said to be the one way out of dependency."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBreakingHabitByChangingScriptAndSceneryCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromHarmfulHabitsCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLossOfIndividualPathCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loss of the individual path"@en, "Verlust des eigenen Wegs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Harvesting human energy is not itself the worst; the gravest danger is that the structure erases its members' individual paths, makes them want only what serves it and lowers their awareness further, aiming at a single informational field."@en ;
    skos:note "Full escape from civilisation is said to be no longer possible for modern people; communities in the wild are not judged."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOasisOfNatureAmidCivilisationCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Oasis of nature amid civilisation"@en, "Naturoase inmitten der Zivilisation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: use as few harmful products as possible, substituting natural ones; e.g. keep a family plot with garden where you, not the structure, set the norms (digging optional, wild or paved as you choose); in the city, switch to an exclusively organic, natural diet."@en ;
    skos:note "Each person must choose the way that suits them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakeUpBeforeChangingDietCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wake up before changing diet"@en, "Erst erwachen, dann die Ernährung umstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before moving to natural food one must first awaken to the fact that a perfect-looking supermarket apple grown within the structure suits only a full structural element, with the illnesses that go with such food."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingOasisOfNatureAmidCivilisationCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeralCatAsModelTransurferCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The feral cat as model transurfer"@en, "Die verwilderte Katze als Vorbild-Transerfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "From the author's own forest trips: a once-domestic cat gone wild took offered food but kept its distance; the author calls it a true transurfer that knew real freedom and dipped into civilisation without trading its independence. Using civilisation's benefits is fine as long as one does not become dependent; a free individual is recognised by awareness. The author says he himself has escaped the farm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Energy Lords'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Toasts as declaration of intention"@en, "Trinksprüche als Absichtserklärung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alcohol's energy credit raises free energy, i.e. will; its effect depends on where it is aimed: drinking from sorrow deepens it, from joy brings more joy, with fear brings something to fear. The pendulum has no outer intention and cannot materialise a sector, but a person can; by giving the lent energy goodwill in a toast one reverses its polarity, so a toast is a declaration of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as a folk custom whose hidden purpose is a method of shaping reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed by this part (Russian deklaratsiya namereniya). Outer intention: pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFutureTenseWishesDoNotMaterialiseCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Future-tense wishes do not materialise"@en, "Wünsche im Futur verwirklichen sich nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Common error: toasts phrased for the future only turn the energy positive and leave reality untouched; the wish stays a distant promise because the mirror of the world reflects only the present."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Common error: toasts phrased for the future only turn the energy positive and leave reality untouched; the wish stays a distant promise because the mirror of the world reflects only the present; it bears on pmp:TranserfingPresentTenseDeclarationOfIntentionCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFutureTenseAffirmationNeverArrivesCh9: applied to toasts, and grounded in the mirror reflecting only the present."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPresentTenseDeclarationOfIntentionCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Present-tense declaration of intention"@en, "Absichtserklärung im Präsens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: phrase the toast or wish as already true now ('we are' instead of 'we will be'; we are healthy; we have won; our wishes are fulfilled; luck is always with us), accepting that it may sound odd."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDrawingWishesIntoPresentRealityCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing wishes into present reality"@en, "Wünsche in die gegenwärtige Wirklichkeit ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The effect that a declared wish begins at once to be pulled into today's reality instead of being deferred to a tomorrow that never arrives; thought energy so charged shifts one to a life line of matching quality."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPresentTenseDeclarationYieldsRealisationOfWishesCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Present-tense declaration yields realisation of wishes"@en, "Präsens-Erklärung bewirkt Verwirklichung von Wünschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declaring intention in the present tense is said to start drawing the wish into present reality immediately."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPresentTenseDeclarationOfIntentionCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDrawingWishesIntoPresentRealityCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAlcoholAndDrugsAreNoToolForWishingCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Alcohol and drugs are no tool for wishing"@en, "Alkohol und Drogen sind kein Werkzeug zum Wünschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alcohol is a double-edged blade: bigger credit, higher interest, and as debt grows consciousness and so intention drift into a region of the alternatives space detached from reality; drugs are ruled out entirely. Turning a pendulum's negative energy positive is not always possible and not everyone can do it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIntoxicationPsychosisAttunementUnrealisedSectorsCh8: the drift into unreal sectors is tied here to the growing energy debt."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionCh16, pmp:TranserfingPresentTenseDeclarationOfIntentionCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBlackMagicAsBorrowedDarkEnergyCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Black magic as borrowed dark energy"@en, "Schwarze Magie als geliehene dunkle Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Black magic is said to work alike: an evil magician summons dark powers to use their energy to reinforce hostile intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRuleOnPendulumsHookThinkOnlyPositiveCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rule on the pendulum's hook: think only positive"@en, "Regel am Pendelhaken: nur Positives denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you have taken energy credit from a pendulum despite its being never profitable, keep strictly to one rule: while hanging on its hook think solely of positive things."@en ;
    skos:note "That a pendulum's credit never pays is already carried: pmc:TranserfingPendulumNeverConstructive (Stupen' I)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHarnessingTransurfingPendulumCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Harnessing the Transurfing pendulum"@en, "Das Transerfing-Pendel nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: whenever you meet anything about Transurfing, remind yourself that it helps you realise your goals; so attune intention and turn the alternatives flow the right way."@en ;
    skos:note "The Transurfing pendulum is said not to harm, and the declaration may strongly raise its effect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHarnessingTransurfingPendulumYieldsMovementTowardGoalsCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Harnessing the Transurfing pendulum yields movement toward goals"@en, "Transerfing-Pendel nutzen bewirkt Bewegung zum Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reminding oneself that Transurfing helps one's goals is said to turn the alternatives flow toward their realisation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHarnessingTransurfingPendulumCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDrawingWishesIntoPresentRealityCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRidingAnyPendulumWithTargetSlideCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Riding any pendulum with the target slide"@en, "Jedes Pendel mit dem Zielbild reiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: while consuming any pendulum's offer (e.g. a TV series) hold ready the target slide, the picture of what you want; look for some link to your goal in the stream of information, however slight; when it appears state your intention, e.g. that you mean to get a car like the heroes'."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10: the target slide is held during the energy exchange with any pendulum one happens to be consuming."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTargetSlideOnAnyPendulumYieldsRealisationCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide on any pendulum yields realisation of wishes"@en, "Zielbild bei jedem Pendel bewirkt Wunschverwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using the energy exchange with any pendulum to declare one's goal is presented as a way of bringing the goal into reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRidingAnyPendulumWithTargetSlideCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDrawingWishesIntoPresentRealityCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoNegativeThoughtWhileReceivingCreditCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No negative thought while receiving credit"@en, "Kein negativer Gedanke beim Empfang eines Kredits"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the moment of an energy boost worries, problems, despair and fear must be avoided, because the extra energy amplifies them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRidingAnyPendulumWithTargetSlideCh16, pmp:TranserfingDeclaringIntentionDuringSmallEnergyCreditsCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDeclaringDuringSmallCreditsYieldsRealisationCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring during small credits yields realisation"@en, "Erklärung bei kleinen Krediten bewirkt Verwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning a routine smoke or coffee into a declaration of intention is offered as a way to steer reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDeclaringIntentionDuringSmallEnergyCreditsCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDrawingWishesIntoPresentRealityCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclaringIntentionDuringSmallEnergyCreditsCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring intention during small energy credits"@en, "Absicht erklären bei kleinen Energiekrediten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: during a smoke break, coffee or tea do not let thoughts drift; picture coming success as already accomplished, or enjoy the luck you already have regardless of the future; declare that all goes splendidly because you shape your reality by intention and know how to do it."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked to the principle of coordination (pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti); tea ceremonies are said to rest on the same principle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDedicatingOnesFoodToOneselfCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dedicating one's food to oneself"@en, "Das Essen sich selbst widmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: as with grace before meals dedicated to God, also dedicate the food to yourself; serve yourself sincerely and lovingly; address yourself with caring words urging yourself to eat and get well, and remind yourself that no one else will feed you if you do not."@en ;
    skos:note "The practice of saying grace is cited as a widespread custom, not disputed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBodilyFlourishingAndHealingThroughSelfCareCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily flourishing and healing through self-care"@en, "Körperliches Aufblühen und Heilung durch Selbstzuwendung"@de ;
    skos:definition "An unexpected effect on the body, up to the possible disappearance of some illnesses; strongest for those who used to treat themselves with indifference or dislike."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBodyFirstSurprisedThenGladAndBloomingCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Body first surprised, then glad and blooming"@en, "Körper erst überrascht, dann froh und aufblühend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: the body will at first be surprised, then rejoice and bloom like a well-tended flower; striking change for those who had treated themselves coldly."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDedicatingOnesFoodToOneselfCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfDedicationOfFoodYieldsBodilyFlourishingCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-dedication of food yields bodily flourishing"@en, "Selbstwidmung des Essens bewirkt körperliches Aufblühen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loving self-dedication of meals is said to carry great power and to bring remarkable change."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDedicatingOnesFoodToOneselfCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBodilyFlourishingAndHealingThroughSelfCareCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMixedHopeAndFearSpoilGamblersIntentionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed hope and fear spoil the gambler's intention"@en, "Gemischte Hoffnung und Angst verderben die Spielabsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "the usual gambler's thoughts mix wanting, scheming, fear of losing and hope of luck, which is said to be useless."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the usual gambler's thoughts mix wanting, scheming, fear of losing and hope of luck, which is said to be useless; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaration of intention in games of chance"@en, "Absichtserklärung bei Glücksspielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: when placing the stake and throughout play hold a slide of certain winnings; set aside every thought and feeling, including desire, calculation, fear of loss and even hope; keep only an unconditional, detached will to win; declare 'I am a winner' plainly, without reasons, conditions or exclamation."@en ;
    skos:note "Said to apply to stock market, casino or racing; not easy but possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRaisedChancesOfWinningCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Raised chances of winning"@en, "Erhöhte Gewinnchancen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state of detached, unconditional will to have that is said to raise one's chances of success in gambling sharply; one may win once, twice or three times in a session."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGamblingDeclarationYieldsRaisedChancesCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Gambling declaration yields raised chances"@en, "Spielerklärung bewirkt erhöhte Chancen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The detached declaration 'I am a winner' is said to increase chances of winning rapidly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRaisedChancesOfWinningCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWinningStreaksMustEndCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Winning streaks must end"@en, "Gewinnserien enden zwangsläufig"@de ;
    skos:definition "no one can hold importance at a minimum indefinitely, so wins cannot continue; all gambling is energy credit that can quietly become an induced transition ending tragically."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: no one can hold importance at a minimum indefinitely, so wins cannot continue; all gambling is energy credit that can quietly become an induced transition ending tragically; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Induced transition: pmc:TranserfingIndutsirovannyPerekhod (Stupen' I)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLeavingGameAndCuttingTieCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving the game and cutting the tie"@en, "Das Spiel verlassen und die Verbindung kappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: know when to stop; on leaving, sever every link with the pendulum and quench any thought resonating at its frequency; for a while turn attention elsewhere so the game does not cross your mind at all; stop swinging with the pendulum; only when the tie is fully cut start a new session."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the only way to avoid paying interest on the credit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCuttingTheTieBeforeANewSessionCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting the tie before a new session"@en, "Erst die Verbindung kappen, dann eine neue Runde"@de ;
    skos:definition "A new round of play is to begin only once every tie with the game pendulum has been cut and thoughts of the game have stopped; no consequence of skipping is stated beyond the general risk of the induced transition, so the order is prescribed, not a stated necessity."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingLeavingGameAndCuttingTieCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEscapeFromInducedTransitionCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Escape from the induced transition"@en, "Entkommen aus dem induzierten Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Avoiding interest on pendulum credit and not being pulled into the whirl of an induced transition."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Induced transition: pmc:TranserfingIndutsirovannyPerekhod (Stupen' I)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCuttingTieYieldsEscapeFromInducedTransitionCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting the tie yields escape from induced transition"@en, "Verbindung kappen bewirkt Entkommen aus dem Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fully disconnecting from the game pendulum is named the only protection against the induced transition."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLeavingGameAndCuttingTieCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEscapeFromInducedTransitionCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayingWithPendulumIsDangerousCh16 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Playing with a pendulum is dangerous"@en, "Spiel mit einem Pendel ist gefährlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gambling against a pendulum is called a risky and unpredictable venture, since no one has a superhuman detached will to have; a pendulum cannot be beaten, any more than one can outrun one's shadow."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfIntentionInGamesOfChanceCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDanceWithShadowCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dance with a shadow"@en, "Tanz mit einem Schatten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pendulum is likened to an invisible, cold, pitiless shadow without awareness, intention, heart or mind; trying to beat it is chasing one's own shadow. The only meaningful options are to quit the dangerous game or to launch one's own venture and be favoured by a pendulum. Efforts to win belong to inner intention, which sees nothing beyond the obvious."@en ;
    skos:note "Gives the chapter its title."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBecomingProducerOfOnesOwnGameCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming producer of one's own game"@en, "Produzent des eigenen Spiels werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: stop chasing; look around; drop narrow inner intention; set off independently in your own direction; be yourself; claim the privilege of shaping your reality at your own discretion, knowing that only you can grant or withhold it; then the pendulum must follow you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMasterOfGameCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Master of the game"@en, "Herr des Spiels"@de ;
    skos:definition "The position in which the pendulum must keep pace with the person, not the reverse; one becomes producer of the shadow dance and shapes one's own reality at will."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnDirectionYieldsMasteryOfGameCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own direction yields mastery of the game"@en, "Eigene Richtung bewirkt Herrschaft über das Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stopping the chase and going one's own way is said to reverse roles with the pendulum."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBecomingProducerOfOnesOwnGameCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMasterOfGameCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeYourselfBeforeStartingYourOwnGameCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Be yourself before starting your own game"@en, "Erst man selbst sein, dann das eigene Spiel beginnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Starting one's own game is said to require being oneself, i.e. granting oneself permission to be oneself (restated in the summary)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingMasterOfGameCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumMustTakeYouUpBeforeSuccessCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A pendulum must take you up before success"@en, "Erfolg erst, wenn ein Pendel einen aufgreift"@de ;
    skos:definition "Permission to be producer is not enough: however wise or masterly, no one learns of a work unless a strong pendulum carries it; outstanding works in culture, science and art gain interest only if a new pendulum arises or an existing one profits. To become a star one must know how to use pendulum features."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterOrStarCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingUsingPendulums ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without a powerful pendulum the work remains unknown and unsuccessful, however remarkable." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFadedPendulumsLeaveWorksUnwantedCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faded pendulums leave works unwanted"@en, "Erloschene Pendel lassen Werke unbeachtet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Works once hugely popular lose their public although their qualities remain, because the pendulums that carried them have weakened or gone out; many cultural achievements that would satisfy any present standard find no market for that reason alone."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPopularityWavesAndCharismaOfEpochCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Popularity waves and the charisma of an epoch"@en, "Popularitätswellen und das Charisma einer Epoche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fashion and popularity are said always to be made by pendulums. Using the Beatles and Abba, the author traces a wave: long obscurity with a small loyal following, a sudden rise, a lull, then an overwhelming wave, later displaced by new pendulums. An epoch's charisma is said to be drawn in, cloud-like, out of the alternatives space by collective intention: fans' 'I like it' is synchronised by a pendulum into 'we like it', driving realisation toward the sectors where everyone likes it until critical mass is passed."@en ;
    skos:note "Biographical details taken from Hunter Davies's authorised Beatles biography; the band's chant ritual is quoted there, but the author says determination was not what brought success."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFashionOriginatesPeopleFreePendulumsX10: fashion is said always to be made by pendulums, an epoch's charisma being drawn in by collective intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSettingTrendsByBeingOneselfCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Setting trends by being oneself"@en, "Trends setzen, indem man man selbst ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: exercise your lawful right to be yourself, not glancing over your shoulder at others; stop chasing your shadow; set out independently on your own path; announce your declaration of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the only way to convey one's individuality to the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeingOneselfYieldsTrendsettingCh16 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Being oneself yields trendsetting"@en, "Selbstsein bewirkt Trendsetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Going one's own way and declaring intention is said to force pendulums to follow and make one a star."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSettingTrendsByBeingOneselfCh16 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterOrStarCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterOrStarCh16 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a trendsetter or star"@en, "Trendsetter oder Star werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communicating one's unique individuality to the world so that pendulums, unable to tolerate uniqueness, must make one a star; an individual 'cloud' in the alternatives space is said to be prepared and waiting."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterFavouriteOwnPendulumX10: pendulums, intolerant of uniqueness, are said to be forced to make one a star, and an individual cloud to wait ready in the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Declaration of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Summary'
#

pmc:TranserfingTwoLawsOfThePendulumCh16 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two laws of the pendulum"@en, "Zwei Gesetze des Pendels"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author sets two laws of the pendulum side by side: by the first it inflames the energy of whatever conflict balanced forces bring about; by the second it does everything it can to keep stable the structure on which it depends. The predatory order of nature is traced to the first; the coordination of every organised structure to the second."@en ;
    skos:note "First law: pmc:TranserfingLawOfThePendulumCh16; second law: pmc:TranserfingStabilisingTheStructureCh16."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Summary'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingParticipatingSpectatorBeforeFreedomFromStructureCh16 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Participating spectator before freedom from the structure"@en, "Teilnehmender Zuschauer vor Freiheit von der Struktur"@de ;
    skos:definition "The summary states that release from the structure's zombifying effect requires acting as a participating spectator."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulumManipulationCh16 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingGainingConfidenceInsideGroupWithoutSubmittingCh16 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Summary'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclaringIntentionAtEveryEnergyCreditCh16 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring intention at every energy credit"@en, "Bei jedem Energiekredit die Absicht erklären"@de ;
    skos:definition "General rule from the summary: on receiving any energy credit, make a declaration of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Generalises A1-109, A1-118 and A1-121."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVI Dances with Shadows, section 'Summary'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV:
# Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), part 2: chapter XVII The Dreams of the Gods,
# to the closing SUMMARY. Kept apart from traditions/transerfing.ttl, which
# declares the tradition and its works. Read in the English translation of the
# combined edition (Ves, 2012); the text layer has no page numbers, every
# source names chapter and section heading.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 96 records, B 151;
# 25 records of B without counterpart in A: 4 added, 19 covered, 2 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 2 nodes both passes missed (the waking dream
# as a term, and the new worldview template as prior to directing the dream of
# life) and refiled several: the God of the dream theatre from a naming to a
# concept, two cautions without a warning folded into concepts, the polemics
# as concepts, one prerequisite from presentation to prescribed order, the
# practice of respect for living beings as the author's own norm, the plant
# experiments split from the author's claim that plants have souls. Stupen'
# I-III (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, -2.ttl, -3.ttl) are not
# restated: 9 records whose claim a node there already carries are left out
# and linked; 24 nodes that restate an earlier node with a difference say so
# in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingWakingDreamCh17,
# pmc:TranserfingDreamTheatreCh17, pmc:TranserfingAssemblagePointCh17 (the
# Toltec cocoon and assemblage point as Zeland combines them with Transurfing),
# pmc:TranserfingTwoSidesOfRealityCh17. The terms typed by part 1 (chapter
# XVI) are not referenced. Bronnikov, the neurophysiologists, the cosmonaut's
# diary, Castaneda and Mares and the scriptural saying are authorities the
# author interprets, so textual; nothing is claimed as received. The pupils'
# abilities, the past-life cases and the plant and DNA experiments are
# third-party ascriptions.
#

#
# ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'
#

pmc:TranserfingTwoSidesOfRealityCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The two sides of reality"@en, "Die zwei Seiten der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is treated as a mirror with a tangible physical face and a metaphysical face that escapes perception yet is held to be no less objective. The world is said to show itself as whatever the observer takes it for (particle or wave, mass or energy), so rival schools each find confirmation; science studies the reflected side, esotericism tries to glimpse the hidden one."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMirrorOfAlternatives: there physical reality reflects one alternative; here reality itself is a two-faced mirror whose hidden face is as objective as the material one, and which assents to every model put to it (compare pmc:TranserfingChosenWorldviewManifests)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAlternativesSpaceAsStationaryMatrixCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alternatives space as stationary matrix"@en, "Variantenraum als stationäre Matrix"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the far face of the mirror lies the alternatives space, holding the scripts of every possible event, as countless as points on a graph; a physical event realises one of them. Seen from three dimensions it is everywhere and nowhere, perhaps beyond the visible universe, perhaps in a coffee cup. It is set apart from the popular notion of a shared information field through which data travel between objects: it is a fixed matrix that defines what can occur."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingInformationFieldMatrix and pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoVariantov: new is the explicit contrast with a field that transmits data between objects, and the claim that the space lies outside the third dimension."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamingAsTheSoulsFlightCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreaming as the soul's flight"@en, "Träumen als Flug der Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the conscious psyche is called mind and the subconscious soul, dreaming is a journey of the soul through the alternatives space; its pictures are not made up by the mind but truly seen, scenes of past or future stored like frames on a reel. Time, the unfolding of events, appears only as that reel moves; the mind acts as observer and generator of ideas."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoSnovideniy: the dream as real seeing recurs; new are the film-reel image of stored frames and the derivation of time from the reel's movement. Memory as stored addresses and discovery as received through the soul, set out in the same passage with an Einstein remark, are carried by pmc:TranserfingMemoryAsAddressesCh7 and pmc:TranserfingOldBricks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDirectVisionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct vision"@en, "Direktes Sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing with eyes shut as well as open, through walls, below ground and over great distances as if through a telescope. Explained as the brain, by way of the soul, tuning to the store of the whole mould of physical reality, so that where an object physically is no longer matters; neurophysiologists are cited as finding that signal processing is registered without any point of entry."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported of children trained at Vyacheslav Bronnikov's International Academy of Human Development; the author holds it entirely possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRetainingHugeVolumesOfInformationCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Memorising very large amounts of information"@en, "Einprägen sehr großer Informationsmengen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to commit vast quantities of information to memory, listed among the gifts of Bronnikov's pupils next to clairvoyance and direct vision."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHigherConsciousnessAsTheAlternativesSpaceCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bronnikov's higher consciousness read as the alternatives space"@en, "Bronnikows höheres Bewusstsein als Variantenraum gelesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bronnikov is cited as placing a higher consciousness outside the human mind, as a surrounding medium to which the conscious mind connects; the author reads this medium as the alternatives space and says the name does not matter: the brain sees that space through the soul, the eyes see physical reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    skos:note "An interpreted quotation, entered as textual attestation of this work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPerceivingTheRealisedSectorCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perceiving the currently realised sector"@en, "Wahrnehmen des gegenwärtig verwirklichten Sektors"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to perceive that part of the alternatives space which is at present manifest as material reality, as against its unrealised parts; physiologically perhaps a kind of synchronisation of the two brain hemispheres."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealisedSectorBeforeDirectVisionCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Perceiving the realised sector before direct vision"@en, "Wahrnehmen des verwirklichten Sektors vor direktem Sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever would develop direct vision must first learn to perceive the sector that is realised now; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingDirectVisionCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPerceivingTheRealisedSectorCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBronnikovExercisesCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bronnikov's exercise system"@en, "Bronnikows Übungssystem"@de ;
    skos:definition "A system of special yet very simple exercises, credited to Bronnikov, by which ordinary people are said to develop direct vision and allied abilities. The chapter gives no steps; readers are pointed to the internet to look it up and try it."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a pointer only: no step can be performed from this text; kept because the text ties it to stated capacities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBronnikovExercisesYieldDirectVisionCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Bronnikov's exercises yield direct vision"@en, "Bronnikows Übungen bringen direktes Sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercises are said to let ordinary individuals acquire direct vision and the related abilities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBronnikovExercisesCh17 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDirectVisionCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnrealisedAlternativesMisleadClairvoyantsCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unrealised alternatives mislead clairvoyants"@en, "Unverwirklichte Varianten führen Hellseher in die Irre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because alternatives are endless, a seer may glimpse events that never happened and never will, so prognoses go wrong; hence nobody can know one's future, since none can tell which alternative will be realised, and a dream likewise carries no guarantee of showing the sector that becomes physical. The author welcomes this: the future is not fatally fixed."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: clairvoyance misses whenever the seen sector is one that stays unrealised; it bears on pmc:TranserfingClairvoyance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWhyClairvoyantsErr: the cause of error recurs; new are the conclusions that no one can foretell a person's future, that dreams give no guarantee either, and that this is good news because the future stays open."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingOnesOwnRealityAsTheTaskCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating one's own reality as the task"@en, "Die eigene Wirklichkeit erschaffen als Aufgabe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing is said not to aim at regretful looks back or anxious looks ahead, but at deliberately making one's own reality; thought energy can, under certain conditions, materialise a chosen sector (pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector)."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingControlOfDestiny: the promise of steering life is now set against regret over the past and worry about the future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIndirectMethodsForOuterIntentionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Indirect methods for outer intention"@en, "Indirekte Methoden für die äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Modern people are said to have lost the outer intention that old civilisations, Atlantis among them, possessed; its remnants survive in scattered esoteric teachings that are hard to apply to daily life. Transurfing claims indirect methods that set outer intention (pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie) to work, provided certain rules are kept; consciousness can reach it in a particular state."@en ;
    skos:note "Outer intention, its location outside the person and the pyramids, and its loss in modern man are carried by pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie and pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionAtrophiedCh7; that it arises where soul and reason agree by pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma and pmc:TranserfingHeartMindUnityBeforeControlOuterCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulatingTheReflectionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulating the reflection"@en, "Am Spiegelbild hantieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The everyday mind tries in vain to alter the mirrored picture; wishing alone does not make the wished-for real. What has to change is the image itself, defined as the focus and character of one's thoughts, which needs knowledge of how the two-sided mirror works and breaking the solid block of what passes for common sense."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: working on the reflection rather than the image leaves the desired unrealised."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMirrorOfAlternatives: the image is now defined as the direction and nature of one's thoughts, and common sense is named as what must be undermined."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDualCorrespondencesOfRealityCh17 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dual correspondences of the two sides"@en, "Doppelte Entsprechungen der beiden Seiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author pairs the faces of reality: soul with the alternatives space, mind with the material world; inner intention with material reality, outer intention with the virtual sectors. Where both meet on the mirror's surface, so-called paranormal events arise; wave-particle duality, the creation and annihilation of particles in a vacuum, and above all the human being, uniting matter and spirit, are given as border cases. When a possibility is realised the mirror shows a symmetrical image, sector on one face, its material form on the other; all beings balance on the edge, body and mind on the material side, soul bound to the alternatives space."@en ;
    skos:note "Inner and outer intention: pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie, pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPotentialBoundedOnlyByIntentionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Potential bounded only by intention"@en, "Nur durch Absicht begrenztes Potential"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because humans dwell on the face of a giant mirror, with the universe of matter at one side and the dark eternity of alternatives at the opposite one, keeping to the physical side alone is called short-sighted; the reader is promised to learn the dual mirror, do what seemed impossible and find that one's potential has no limit but intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Two Sides to Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'
#

pmc:TranserfingTheatreOfMasksCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Theatre of masks"@en, "Theater der Masken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beings come from the alternatives space and return to it between lives as an actor goes to the wings to change costume, then comes back in a new guise having forgotten every former part, so absorbed in the role as to lose sense of who they are; at times the veil drops and they realise they have been on this stage before."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRecallOfPastLivesCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recall of past lives"@en, "Erinnerung an frühere Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remembering former incarnations, with details such as speaking a language never learned (Old Aramaic, a Bengali dialect), recognising a house, places and people; reported mostly of young children, without hypnosis, and of some adults, and under hypnotic regression six incarnations over two millennia, checked by historians. The author concludes reincarnation can hardly be doubted."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Cases from Ian Stevenson's collection of over 2,500 and from Andrzej Donimirski's account of the hypnotist Arnold Blacksman; outcomes of narrated cases, not signs of success."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAccessPastLifeInformationX10: there the author left past lives open and out of scope; here he holds reincarnation all but proven."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessBlockedNotMemoryErasedCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness blocked, not memory erased"@en, "Blockierte Bewusstheit statt gelöschter Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Past lives, chiefly remembered in early childhood, are not wiped out but cut off by blocked awareness, as are most memories before about age four. Children are said to be far more aware than adults; it is adults, sunk in a subconscious daydream, who lose access. The author admits he cannot say why such recall is so rare and confined to so few."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingFromTheDaydreamBeforePastLifeRecallCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking from life's daydream before past-life recall"@en, "Erwachen aus dem Tagtraum des Lebens vor der Erinnerung früherer Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anyone is said to be able to recall former incarnations once they wake from the daydream that life is; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRecallOfPastLivesCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorldviewTemplateAndTwoLevelsOfAwarenessCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Worldview template and the two levels of awareness"@en, "Weltbildschablone und die zwei Ebenen der Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reborn, the soul stays in the background and the mind leads; the mind starts as a blank sheet onto which a template of self and everyday reality is printed, and the more detailed it is, the wider the gulf between heart and mind. Awareness has two levels, attention and perception; in infancy perception is still unclouded, so the infant's intuition and clairvoyance are unobstructed and the world is seen as it is."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTemplatePerceptionCh9: new are the blank sheet stamped at birth, the gulf between heart and mind growing with the template's detail, and the split of awareness into attention and perception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCapturedAttentionNarrowsAwarenessCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Captured attention narrows awareness"@en, "Gefesselte Aufmerksamkeit verengt die Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreaming adults squeeze the newborn into their narrow frame by curbing its freedom and holding its attention with orders; once attention is captured, outlook shrinks, awareness goes and the person slides into a state near unconscious dreaming, eyes as if glued to their shoes, bedded in false stereotypes of how things should be. The better a child learns the rules of material life, the more its awareness sinks, and with it the power to sway events and sense the metaphysical side."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: attention held to a few objects and learned material rules lower awareness and the ability to influence events."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeStatesOfDreamingAwarenessCh17 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three states of dreaming awareness"@en, "Drei Zustände der träumenden Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author orders three states: non-lucid dreaming, where attention and perception are programmed to the full and the dream happens to one according to fears and expectations; lucid dreaming, with heightened awareness and control by will; and ordinary waking, where awareness falls again and life becomes an unconscious waking dream. Raising awareness is spoken of in rungs and half rungs."@en ;
    skos:note "Lucid dreaming: pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingDreamCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The waking dream"@en, "Der Wachtraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordinary waking life is held to be an unconscious dream: life just happens, attention and perception are held by problems and oppressive thoughts, one is absorbed in cares as in a daydream and lacks a reference point from which to climb a level higher in awareness. A daydreamer does not control the situation but battles with pendulums; this is how people become grown-ups."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed here (part 2). Differs from pmc:TranserfingGameAsUnrecognisedDream: there the pendulum game is a dream not yet recognised; here waking life as such is the dream, defined by the missing reference point."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The half rung of awareness"@en, "Die halbe Stufe der Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A raised waking awareness in which one knows that reality resembles a dream, looks about soberly and acts dispassionately, leaving the stage for the auditorium or remaining on it as a spectator who takes part. Knowing that life allows one to rise a rung, or at least half a rung, can itself serve as the reference point; this half rung is said to suffice for carrying out the other principles and to let one point one's world the right way by intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7: the witness stance recurs; new is its measure as a half rung that is enough for the remaining principles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidDreamControlCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control in the lucid dream"@en, "Steuerung im Klartraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a lucid dream the dreamer can steer events and do the inconceivable, such as flying, so that nothing there is impossible; this is put down to attention and perception being set free, as if one had raised one's head and taken in one's position."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7: new is the reason given, freed attention and perception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRecognisingTheDreamBeforeControlCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising the dream before controlling it"@en, "Den Traum erkennen, bevor man ihn steuert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The powers of the lucid dream arrive only once the dreamer grasps that it is a dream and recalls the point of reference; until then one is wholly at the dream's mercy."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTwoConditionsForDreamControlCh7: the second condition is now remembering one's reference point, not the realisation that anything can be done there."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingLucidDreamControlCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingReferencePointOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The dreamer stays wholly in the dream's power, dependent on circumstances and boxed in by conditioning." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReferencePointOfAwarenessCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reference point of awareness"@en, "Bezugspunkt der Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dream and reality are relative to each other; mastery of a dream comes from being aware of oneself in it relative to physical reality, the point to which one returns on waking. Waking reality lacks such a point: at death one goes back to the initial point of reference, and at each rebirth forgets it in the next dream of life. Remembering who one really is would make one aware that the dream of life can be directed."@en ;
    skos:note "The origin of this initial point: pmc:TranserfingGodAlmightyAsTheInitialReferencePointCh17."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUncontrolledThoughtFlowInWakingCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uncontrolled flow of thought in waking"@en, "Ungesteuerter Gedankenfluss im Wachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In waking, awareness drops: thoughts leap from topic to topic, what worries or irritates rules consciousness, and the worst expectations and reflexive negative reactions shape reality regardless of will. Wishes stay unmet, dreams fail, fears come true as if out of spite, and life unfolds at random rather than as one wants."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: thought left to run uncontrolled lets fears and worst expectations shape events; it bears on pmp:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowCh17."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChildMasterOfItsGameCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The child as master of its game"@en, "Das Kind als Herr seines Spiels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing at every moment that it is only playing, the child keeps importance low, acts without passion and watches like a spectator; adults, for whom life is serious business, become captives of their games and of circumstance the moment they take them in earnest and let the mind be absorbed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingImportanceAsProjection: the child's harmony recurs; new is its explanation by awareness that it is a game, the source of low importance (pmc:TranserfingVazhnost) and of the observer's stance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSupplementingTheWorldviewTemplateCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supplementing the worldview template; altered states"@en, "Ergänzung der Weltbildschablone; veränderte Zustände"@de ;
    skos:definition "The template is like a stencil pressed into the mind that cannot be corrected or erased; one can only add a second one, which needs tearing the mind away from the first, possible in altered states such as sleep or under psychotropic substances. Normally heart and mind are tuned together to a realised sector; intoxication loosens the mind's grip so the soul drifts to near, unrealised sectors and familiar streets look strange; in non-lucid sleep it reaches very remote sectors, from paradise to worlds of clanking machines or slaughterhouses, which are called unrealised but real."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIntoxicationPsychosisAttunementUnrealisedSectorsCh8: new are the stencil that can only be supplemented, altered states as the moment the mind can be torn from it, and the grading of drift by distance (near under alcohol, far in sleep)."@en ;
    skos:note "The author hopes no one ever lands in a physical world of a nightmare's kind; a cosmonaut's diary (Gennady Strekalov) on strange dreams in orbit is cited as support for the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNewTemplateBeforeDirectingLifeCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A new template before directing the dream of life"@en, "Eine neue Schablone, bevor man den Lebenstraum lenkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming able to steer the dream that life is, by remembering who one is, is called very hard because it first requires changing the worldview template; no consequence of skipping is named beyond the difficulty."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingLifeAsALucidDreamCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingSupplementingTheWorldviewTemplateCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAssemblagePointCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Toltec cocoon and assemblage point combined with Transurfing"@en, "Toltekischer Kokon und Montagepunkt, mit Transurfing verbunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taken from Carlos Castaneda's and Theun Mares' books, said to render the teaching of the Toltecs, called the last people out of Atlantis: a person is enveloped in a shining cocoon of energy threads that meet near the shoulder blades in one focus, the assemblage point, whose position sets how one perceives. Joined with Transurfing: in its habitual place perception matches the corresponding realised sector; shifted aside, the synchronism breaks and unrealised regions are perceived; dreams are governed by such shifts."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed here (part 2). An interpreted reading of named authors, entered as textual attestation of this work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClairvoyanceFromAWanderingAssemblagePointCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clairvoyance from a wandering assemblage point"@en, "Hellsehen durch einen wandernden Montagepunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In most people the points sit firmly; when the focus is unsettled for whatever reason and they begin to drift, clairvoyant abilities are said to appear."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStuckAssemblagePointCh17 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A stuck assemblage point"@en, "Ein festsitzender Montagepunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The focus of perception must not only move aside but come back to its former place; if it stays fixed out of its natural place, the mind changes in the way usually called madness."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingClairvoyanceFromAWanderingAssemblagePointCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionalShiftingOfTheAssemblagePointCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting the assemblage point at will"@en, "Willentliches Verschieben des Montagepunkts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those able to move their assemblage point deliberately are said to shape reality and to be lucid dreamers."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReferencePointBeforeShiftingAbilityCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Return to the reference point before the shifting ability"@en, "Rückkehr zum Bezugspunkt vor der Fähigkeit des Verschiebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability appears by itself once one returns to the reference point relative to reality, that is, becomes aware of who one really is; this is called no easy task."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIntentionalShiftingOfTheAssemblagePointCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingReferencePointOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnlightenmentAsABirdsEyeViewCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enlightenment as a bird's-eye view"@en, "Erleuchtung als Vogelperspektive"@de ;
    skos:definition "Likened to wandering lost in a strange city's winding lanes and then rising into the sky, where the whole lies below and the way to the goal is as plain as a line on one's palm; those known to have reached it are said to be countable on one hand's fingers."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEnlightenmentOnenessWorldCh9: there enlightenment is oneness with the world; here it is an overview that makes the path obvious, and is called extremely rare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReachOfTheMethodCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reach of the method"@en, "Reichweite der Methode"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing will not raise anyone to the bird's height of enlightenment but shows a way one can walk blindfold. Material realisation does not follow the will fluidly as in a dream; it is sluggish like tar, yet can still be moved through the principles of Transurfing."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the limits of the method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWakeUpCallCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The wake-up call"@en, "Der Weckruf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Amid everyday activity (walking down a street, talking, doing chores) call out to yourself to wake up; look around and take in soberly what is going on; remind yourself that reality resembles a dream. Keep calling yourself awake on purpose, regularly, until it has become a habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7: the rousing of oneself recurs; new are the explicit call, the reminder that reality resembles a dream, and repetition until it is habitual. Coming down into the auditorium, acting dispassionately and renting oneself out, named in the same passage, are carried by pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7, pmp:TranserfingRentYourselfOut and pmc:TranserfingAuditoriumYieldsAwarenessCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling the flow of thought"@en, "Den Gedankenfluss steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep a steady watch on the stream of your thoughts so as to hold your level of awareness; at first by deliberate effort, until it turns into habit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakeUpCallYieldsHalfRungCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The wake-up call yields the half rung"@en, "Der Weckruf bringt die halbe Stufe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeatedly calling oneself awake in the midst of daily life is said to raise and keep the half rung of awareness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWakeUpCallCh17 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowYieldsHalfRungCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Control of thought keeps the half rung"@en, "Steuerung der Gedanken hält die halbe Stufe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consistent control of the thought stream is called essential for keeping one's level of awareness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowCh17 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessBecomesAutomaticCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness becomes automatic"@en, "Bewusstheit wird selbsttätig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once control of thought and the call to wake have turned into habit, they run by themselves and cost no effort, just as someone who has woken inside a dream needs no effort to stay aware of dreaming."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingWakeUpCallCh17 and pmp:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowCh17."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNavigatingLifeWithoutProblemsCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Navigating life without problems"@en, "Das Leben ohne Probleme durchqueren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving with confidence through life's labyrinth and steering clear of all kinds of trouble, even with eyes closed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCorePrinciplesYieldProblemFreeNavigationCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The three main principles yield problem-free navigation"@en, "Die drei Hauptprinzipien bringen problemloses Durchqueren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lowering importance, moving with the flow of alternatives, and coordination, named here the chief principles, are said to carry one with confidence through life's maze."@en ;
    skos:note "The three principles are entered as practices in Stupen' I and III and are not retyped here."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance, pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow, pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingNavigatingLifeWithoutProblemsCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHalfRungBeforeTheOtherPrinciplesCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The half rung before the other principles"@en, "Die halbe Stufe vor den übrigen Prinzipien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking up is named the first thing to do; the half rung gained by it is said to suffice for applying the remaining principles. No consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance, pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow, pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFromWakingToThePrinciplesCh17 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From waking to the principles"@en, "Vom Erwachen zu den Prinzipien"@de ;
    skos:definition "The chapter orders the work: first wake up and know that reality is dreamlike; then come down into the auditorium as observer and keep watch over the thoughts; then, from that half rung, apply the lowering of importance, going with the flow and coordination."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:TranserfingWakeUpCallCh17 ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7 ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:TranserfingControllingTheThoughtFlowCh17 ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow ;
    rdf:_6 pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Waking comes first, the observer's stance and watch over thought hold it, and only from the half rung so reached are the three main principles carried out." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodAlmightyAsTheInitialReferencePointCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God Almighty as the initial reference point"@en, "Gott der Allmächtige als anfänglicher Bezugspunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the alternatives space holds, somewhere, a reference point that precedes this life, relative to which reality is a dream, its origin is held to be God Almighty himself; every being's soul is a part of God and every life a dream. Whether God has a reference point of his own is left to those who live on hope, as unknowable as what lies beyond the visible universe."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "God Almighty" ;
    pm:nameRole "origin of the reference point prior to life, of whom every soul is a part" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Waking Dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'
#

pmc:TranserfingAgainstTheSelfRighteousnessOfBelieversCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the self-righteousness of believers"@en, "Gegen die Selbstgerechtigkeit der Gläubigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pious are said to have long credited themselves with every virtue and charged the godless with sin, while atrocities were and are committed to please God by persecuting dissenters. Faith does not of itself make anyone righteous; the believers' certainty is a support point gained inside the pendulum of religion, which offers trust in mercy, forgiveness, absolution through repentance, hope of help and belonging, while atheists must rely on their own strength."@en ;
    skos:note "A polemic; only the author's side is read, so entered as a concept. Religions as pendulums: pmc:TranserfingReligionsAsPendulumsCh13."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEgoAndItsTwoEscapesCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The ego and its two escapes"@en, "Das Ego und seine zwei Auswege"@de ;
    skos:definition "Often not love but fear and insecurity drive people towards God; they are really fleeing their ego. The ego is born of dependent relationships, comparing oneself with others and finding oneself imperfect, and seeks only to assert its significance; denied, it is offended and causes inner discomfort. One then either gives it free rein (the egoist) or smothers it (the altruist who forsakes care of his own soul, or by turning to aggression the criminal or cynic); devout and fallen are opposite poles of one process. The ego itself pushes the search for God, and seeking God to shed the ego is the road of inner importance, present whenever one hands oneself over to others' judgement."@en ;
    skos:note "Inner importance: pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodWithinCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God within"@en, "Gott im Inneren"@de ;
    skos:definition "God is held to dwell inside a person, not outside; he governs the world through his particle in each being. Worshipping an abstract symbol, the ego turns away from the true God, that is, from its own soul."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOneSpirit: the indwelling particle recurs; new is the claim that worship of an outer symbol turns one from God, who is one's soul."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "God" ;
    pm:nameRole "particle present in every living being, identified with one's soul" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJesusAsHigherManifestationCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus as a higher manifestation of the Lord"@en, "Jesus als höhere Erscheinung des Herrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Named, with Mohammed, Buddha and Krishna, as a higher manifestation of the Lord; ordinary people are lesser manifestations of the same Lord, so that worship of one by another is called pointless."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingJesusAsExemplarCh7: there Jesus is the measure of outer intention; here he is one higher manifestation of the Lord among four."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus" ;
    pm:nameRole "higher manifestation of the Lord" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMohammedAsHigherManifestationCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Mohammed as a higher manifestation of the Lord"@en, "Mohammed als höhere Erscheinung des Herrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held, with Jesus, Buddha and Krishna, to be a higher manifestation of the Lord, of whom ordinary people are lesser manifestations."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Mohammed" ;
    pm:nameRole "higher manifestation of the Lord" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBuddhaAsHigherManifestationCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Buddha as a higher manifestation of the Lord"@en, "Buddha als höhere Erscheinung des Herrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held, with Jesus, Mohammed and Krishna, to be a higher manifestation of the Lord, of whom ordinary people are lesser manifestations."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Buddha" ;
    pm:nameRole "higher manifestation of the Lord" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
