pmp:TranserfingReturningToSelfCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Returning to oneself"@en, "Rückkehr zu sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop checking what others think and stop offering yourself up for their judgement; do not heed those who urge you to remake yourself to their standards and to copy them; face yourself, accept yourself as you are, be yourself and claim your right to be right."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the true path to God, as against serving an abstract God, which means abandoning one's soul. The demand to copy others is the pendulum rule typed in part 1 of Stupen' IV; compare pmc:TranserfingDoNotFollowOthersPathsX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfSufficiencyAndIntegralPersonalityCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-sufficiency and the integral personality"@en, "Selbstgenügsamkeit und die ganzheitliche Persönlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state in which, the need to check others' opinion being gone, the ego is said to cease and only the integral personality remains."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaVazhnosti: self-sufficiency recurs; new is that it dissolves the ego and leaves the integral personality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReturningToSelfYieldsSelfSufficiencyCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Returning to oneself yields self-sufficiency"@en, "Rückkehr zu sich selbst bringt Selbstgenügsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dropping the need to consult others' opinion is said to make one self-sufficient and to end the ego."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReturningToSelfCh17 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSelfSufficiencyAndIntegralPersonalityCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheosophyForcedOnNoOneCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A theosophy forced on no one"@en, "Eine niemandem aufgezwungene Theosophie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author calls this the theosophy of Transurfing, imposed on nobody: he proclaims no absolute truths, only tries to uncover certain regularities, and leaves each reader to draw conclusions."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the doctrine is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMarksOfReligiousPendulumZealotsCh17 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Marks of religious pendulum zealots"@en, "Kennzeichen eifernder Anhänger religiöser Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Zealous followers of the pendulum of religion are told from genuine priests by their hostile opposition to every other dogma and their aggressive pressure, which betrays them at once; conflicts over religion persist because the pendulum's first law has not been done away with."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMarksOfDestructivePendulum: the marks of opposition and aggression are now applied to religious adherents and used to tell them from genuine priests."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingReligionsAsPendulumsCh13 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReligionAsMediatedCommunicationCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Religion as communication through a mediator"@en, "Religion als Verkehr mit Gott über einen Mittler"@de ;
    skos:definition "Religion is described as contact with God through a priest, who cannot be done without at baptism, wedding and burial. The author asks whether God would turn away a child not baptised in time, whether all are not his children if a particle of the Creator is in each, and whether anyone needs a go-between with their own mother or father; each must answer for themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "A polemic; only the author's side is read, so entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAsceticismHookCh17 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The hook of asceticism"@en, "Der Haken der Askese"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pendulum of religion demands that adherents renounce worldly pleasure, and spiritual paths are commonly tied to asceticism and to the idea that the enlightened lose interest in earthly things. Do not be caught on that hook: everyone can and must go on looking after material wellbeing, comfort and welfare."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCaptureBySpiritualPendulumCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCaptureBySpiritualPendulumCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Capture by a spiritual pendulum"@en, "Gefangenschaft bei einem spirituellen Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever stops caring for material wellbeing shows they are wholly in the power of an idea, most likely of a pendulum, be it religious, philosophical or another so-called spiritual one; by the pendulums' second law it makes adherents devote themselves to the structure, they lose interest in all else and may fancy themselves devoted to their soul or in conversation with God, while the soul of such an enlightened one is locked away as in a weighty box and cannot voice its needs."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: neglect of material wellbeing marks capture by a pendulum of religion or philosophy (pmc:TranserfingMayatnik)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstLifeAsPreparationForTheHereafterCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against life as preparation for the hereafter"@en, "Gegen das Leben als Vorbereitung aufs Jenseits"@de ;
    skos:definition "That the soul comes into matter to prepare for life afterwards is dismissed as rubbish: it comes anyway and will return to the spiritual world in time. Life in a body is a singular opportunity for the soul to enjoy what the world of matter offers; total devotion to worship, a monastic cell and long hours of prayer are no service to God but distance one from him and deny him the joy of a full life, like keeping a child from play to make it cram."@en ;
    skos:note "A polemic; only the author's side is read, so entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodsIntentionToExperienceCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God's intention to experience"@en, "Gottes Absicht zu erfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Creator is said to have brought forth many realities by way of living beings, which embody him, so as to experience every side of his creation; that is why his children are sent into matter and gives them freedom of action to enjoy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingTheLayerOfOnesWorldCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the layer of one's world"@en, "Die Schicht der eigenen Welt erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Man's original gift of forming his own world layer by drawing potential alternatives out of the metaphysical side into physical reality. The pendulum of religion is said to teach that man is incapable and God almighty, wanting only obedient, serviceable cogs for its machine; pendulums have worn away awareness of this power and replaced the meaning of life with worship, so that God's children have forgotten their own power and magnificence."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLayerOfOnesWorld: there all beings contribute to reality; here forming one's layer is a power given at the origin and eroded by pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoCreationAsServiceToGodCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Co-creation as service to God"@en, "Mitschöpfung als Dienst an Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "God hardly needs worship, any more than parents want it from their children rather than friendship; the purpose of life and of serving God is to create together with him. Believing in God's existence is not understanding him, and prayer does not by itself open communication: the Lord's language is creation, one speaks with him by shaping the layer of one's reality, and he rejoices when one rejoices in it. Belief in God is first belief in oneself as a creator; as far as one believes in one's own potential one fulfils the scriptural word that it be done according to one's faith. The author calls this a matter of choice, not argument."@en ;
    skos:note "An interpreted scriptural quotation, textual attestation of this work. Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstUnshakeableFaithCh13: there the faith saying was read against the doctrine of unwavering faith; here it is fulfilled by believing in one's own creative potential."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Children of God'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'
#

pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityAsThePrimordialMotiveCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control of reality as the primordial motive"@en, "Steuerung der Wirklichkeit als Urmotiv"@de ;
    skos:definition "The root motive of every being's behaviour is the need to manage its own life on its own terms; any purposeful process reduces to an attempt to control its immediate reality. Making and shaping reality is the aim of all life and plainly God's leading function; what God's intention is follows from this: not judging, rewarding, punishing, granting wishes, ruling or caring for people, but controlling reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReligionsSubstitutionsAndAtheismCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Religion's substitutions, and atheism"@en, "Die Ersetzungen der Religion, und der Atheismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Religion is charged with a chain of substitutes: service replaced by worship, God's evident existence by blind faith, man declared powerless against divine omnipotence, his divine essence reduced to nothing, so that he is like a kidnapped child torn from its parents who forgets origin and purpose. From Creator God became a ruler and judge; since the world shows abuse, unpunished wrongdoers and unanswered prayers, adherents patch the gap with formulas such as God's will or a final reckoning. Atheism is religion in reverse, handing fate to circumstance to be fought; either way man plays the puppet."@en ;
    skos:note "A polemic; only the author's side is read, so entered as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStruggleWithinInnerIntentionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Struggle within inner intention"@en, "Kampf innerhalb der inneren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "However hard one struggles, one stays under pendulums and circumstance until one's actions pass beyond inner intention (pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie). One always receives what one chooses: who believes life is a dense forest must clamber over fallen trees, who dares believe he can reach the sky flies over it; nobody holds one down but oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: action confined to inner intention keeps one under pendulums and circumstances."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingOnesDivineEssenceCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting one's divine essence"@en, "Annahme des eigenen göttlichen Wesens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regarding oneself as a particle and child of God and hence as a creator, despite God's image having been twisted from Creator into a ruler demanding worship."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDivineEssenceBeforeOuterIntentionCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting divine essence before receiving through outer intention"@en, "Annahme des göttlichen Wesens vor dem Empfangen durch äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "One will not believe that one can receive anything without conditions through outer intention unless one accepts one's divine essence; this is called very hard because God's essence has been distorted beyond recognition."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingAcceptingOnesDivineEssenceCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without it one does not believe that one can receive through outer intention." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodRulesThroughAllBeingsCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God rules through all beings"@en, "Gott herrscht durch alle Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nothing happens against God's will, yet he does not reign centrally from a throne but through every living being, each carrying his particle, so that the intention of a single being cannot but coincide with his; by placing a soul in each, he let it govern reality in proportion to its consciousness. Everything has some consciousness, from people to minerals, and takes part in shaping reality: rivers lay their beds, mountains rise, deserts and woods, sea and land compete for territory; the higher the consciousness, the greater the power of control."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOneSpirit: the indwelling particle through which God governs recurs; new are the coincidence of each being's intention with God's and the grading of power to control reality by level of consciousness, down to minerals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLadderOfConsciousnessCh17 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ladder of consciousness"@en, "Leiter des Bewusstseins"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author ranks beings: man on the highest rung, yet only relatively awake; plants as deep sleepers; stones alive in a different temporal dimension. All are dreamers, each with its own wants, goals, rights and purpose, and greater consciousness means greater capacity to control reality."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlantAndDnaExperimentsCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plant and DNA experiments as evidence"@en, "Pflanzen- und DNA-Versuche als Beleg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as evidence for sentience: plants are said to have a kind of nervous system, exchange electric potentials, perceive, communicate, remember and analyse. Cleve Backster's polygraph tests in which a plant learned to tell a harmful from a caring person and reacted even to the thought of harm, reportedly repeated by others; a laboratory plant showing affection for one assistant and jealousy; Peter Gariaev's spectrometer readings in the mid-1980s of a DNA molecule's mood and of phantom radiation persisting forty days after the molecules were destroyed. Official science is said to be sceptical."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlantsAsDeepSleepingDreamersCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plants as deep-sleeping dreamers with souls"@en, "Pflanzen als tief schlafende beseelte Träumer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Plants are held to have souls and to feel delight and suffering much as people do, only in a deep sleep compared with man, like a sleeper smiling at a kind voice; they love those who care for them and thank them with fruit. The author hopes they sleep deeply enough not to feel cruelty as keenly as beings higher up the ladder."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRespectForAllLivingBeingsCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Respect for all living beings"@en, "Achtung vor allen Lebewesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat every living creature with respect and as having equal rights; nobody may regard only himself as ensouled and aware and so treat the rest with neglect or scorn. Examples given: peoples not yet spoiled by pendulum civilisation beg pardon of an animal before slaughter or of a tree before cutting it; Buddhists watch their step to spare insects and keep to the path rather than the grass."@en ;
    skos:note "The examples are ascribed to unspoiled cultures and to Buddhists; the norm itself is the author's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDarwinLeavesVariationUnexplainedCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Darwin leaves variation unexplained"@en, "Darwin lässt die Variation unerklärt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evolution, quantitative change turning gradually into qualitative, was first shown by Darwin through variation and natural selection, but the theory is said to miss what causes variation: selection and heredity only remove or fix traits already there. Jumps, gaps, reversals and wholly new forms such as organs of sight, and the origin of the genetic code, resist an ordered account. The Transurfing answer: variation is shaped by intention."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute with Darwinian theory; only the author's side is read, so entered as a concept. Compare pmc:TranserfingNaturalSelectionNotNecessaryConditionLifeCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionDrivesEvolutionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention drives evolution"@en, "Absicht treibt die Evolution"@de ;
    skos:definition "Striving towards a goal drives evolution, which is the mode of creation God himself chose. Every being from single cells to man creates its layer including itself and holds, paraphrased, the intention to be and behave so as to control reality effectively; this intention materialises matching sectors so new traits appear, as early birds with wing claws went from climbing trees, to gliding, to free flight over many generations. Pendulums act by both their laws, destroying (one species ousting or wiping out another) and stabilising, synchronising one trait across a species' whole range."@en ;
    skos:note "Pendulum: pmc:TranserfingMayatnik."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamTheatreCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The dream theatre"@en, "Das Traumtheater"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world is a dream theatre where God is simultaneously audience, author, director and actor: as audience he watches the play, as actor he lives through all that the beings whose roles he plays live through, seeking to experience everything in this kaleidoscope of dreams. As author and director he lets the play unfold freely by the participants' intention; each contributes to shaping reality, and the whole forms God's dream, woven from the dreams of his manifestations. Why he allows injustice and the pendulums is left unanswered as known only to him."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared system term of Stupen' IV, typed here (part 2). Reclassified from a naming of God to a concept: what is set out is the world-play, not a name."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsAsWorldwideSourceOfEvilCh17 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums as worldwide source of evil"@en, "Pendel als weltweite Quelle des Bösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums are called a worldwide source of evil that have gone far in enslaving human will, wearing away man's knowledge of his power to control reality by thought and even of its possibility, and putting worship in place of co-creation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMayatnik: the energy-information structure recurs; new is its role as the world's source of evil that erased knowledge of man's creative power, and its double part in evolution (pmc:TranserfingIntentionDrivesEvolutionCh17)."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "pendulum" ;
    pm:nameRole "collective energy-information structure, source of evil" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomToShapeRealityByConsciousnessCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom and power to form reality by one's consciousness"@en, "Freiheit und Macht, die Wirklichkeit nach dem Bewusstsein zu formen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The one firm conclusion drawn: every living being received from God freedom and the power to form its own reality in keeping with its consciousness; by the level of consciousness life becomes either an unconscious dream in which one is helpless before circumstance, or a conscious dream that intention can steer. Choice is free for everyone, yet hardly anyone uses the privilege."@en ;
    skos:note "Added on reconciliation: found by pass B only."@en ;
    skos:note "Freedom of choice: pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBlurredIntentionOfUnconsciousDreamingCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Blurred intention of unconscious dreaming"@en, "Verschwommene Absicht des unbewussten Träumens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hardly any beings use intention consciously and constructively, which is why evolution is so slow; in unconscious dreaming one vaguely wants something without knowing what, and intention turns vague and indefinite, so that man is no further on here than animals. Drawn into destructive pendulum games, one gets only the backlash of outer intention, realising one's negative attitude and worst expectations, and otherwise stays confined to inner intention and great effort."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: indefinite intention leaves outer intention working only to realise fears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLifeAsALucidDreamCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life as a lucid dream"@en, "Das Leben als Klartraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person of fairly high awareness can break out of the circle and make of life a lucid dream where reality gives way not only to direct action but to the will as well."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHighAwarenessBeforeLucidLifeCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Raised awareness before life as a lucid dream"@en, "Erhöhte Bewusstheit vor dem Leben als Klartraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Escaping the circle and living life as a lucid dream is credited to awareness raised fairly high; no consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingLifeAsALucidDreamCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHalfRungOfAwarenessCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIntentionAsGodsIntentionCh17 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking one's intention as God's"@en, "Die eigene Absicht als die Gottes nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever you form an intention, regard it as God's intention, so that doubt about its fulfilment has no ground; only claim it as your right. Neither ask, nor demand, nor struggle; just create, shaping your reality by conscious intention. Praying to God is treated as God praying to himself, asking him as asking oneself; one's fears and doubts too are his, and the will is free to choose."@en ;
    skos:note "Compare pmc:TranserfingNoPetitioningHigherPowersCh7 and pmp:TranserfingClaimingThePossibilityCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShapingRealityByConsciousIntentionCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shaping reality by conscious intention"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit durch bewusste Absicht formen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forming a new reality as one wishes without wasting effort on battle with an unyielding world, as God is said to do; by shaping reality by intention one fulfils God's will."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodsIntentionStanceYieldsShapingCh17 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Taking one's intention as God's yields shaping by intention"@en, "Die Absicht als göttlich nehmen bringt Formen durch Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating one's intention as God's and claiming one's right to it is said to remove doubt about its fulfilment and let one create one's reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingIntentionAsGodsIntentionCh17 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingShapingRealityByConsciousIntentionCh17 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoosingTheHardPathCh17 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing the hard path"@en, "Den schweren Weg wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever chooses a hard road must fight through all kinds of obstacles, and inevitably so, being convinced that nothing comes for free; one receives as one believes."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the conviction that everything must be fought for makes the path hard; it bears on pmc:TranserfingShapingRealityByConsciousIntentionCh17."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingPossibilityBeforeShapingCh17 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting the possibility before shaping by intention"@en, "Die Möglichkeit annehmen vor dem Formen durch Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "People can shape reality as God does only if they accept that it can be done; for one who is ready, the rest is technique, taught in the next part of the book. No consequence of skipping is named."@en ;
    skos:note "The acceptance is entered as accepting one's divine essence, the capacity the chapter sets before outer intention."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingShapingRealityByConsciousIntentionCh17 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingAcceptingOnesDivineEssenceCh17 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen4 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (2005), ch. XVII The Dreams of the Gods, section 'The Dream Theatre'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .
